helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149987				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>lines; editing points\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>curves; editing points\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Edit Points bar\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149987				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0227.xhp\" name=\"Edit Points Bar\"\>Edit Points Bar\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3150402				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BEZIER_TOOLBOX\"\>The \<emph\>Edit Points \</emph\>Bar appears when you select a polygon object and click \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3144762				0	hi	दिए गए फंक्शन आपको किसी वक्र के या वक्र में बदले गए वस्तु के बिन्दुओं को संपादन करने देता है. निम्न प्रतीक उपलब्ध हैं:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153105				0	hi	Edit Points				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3159151				0	hi	The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05270000.xhp\" name=\"Edit Points\"\>\<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\>\</link\> icon allows you to activate or deactivate the edit mode for Bézier objects. In the edit mode, individual points of the drawing object can be selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	hi	\<image id=\"img_id3153951\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleobjectbeziermode.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153951\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	hi	Edit Points				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146976				0	hi	Move Points				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierMove\"\>Activates a mode in which you can move points.\</ahelp\> The mouse pointer displays a small empty square when resting on a point. Drag that point to another location. The curve on both sides of the point follows the movement; the section of the curve between the next points changes shape.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481				0	hi	वक्र के आकार को बिना खराब किए पूरे वक्र को अन्यत्र खिसकाने के लिए वक्र में दो बिन्दुओं के बीच या किसी बन्द वक्र पर माउस का संकेतक रख कर माउस बटन दबाएँ और माउस को खींचें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3154096				0	hi	\<image id=\"img_id3149377\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziermove.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149377\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3147397				0	hi	Move Points				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150115				0	hi	Insert Points				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3160478				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierInsert\"\>Activates the insert mode. This mode allows you to insert points.\</ahelp\> You can also move points, just as in the move mode. If, however, you click at the curve between two points and move the mouse a little while holding down the mouse button you insert a new point. The point is a smooth point, and the lines to the control points are parallel and remain so when moved.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3157846				0	hi	If you wish to create a corner point you must first insert either a smooth or a symmetrical point which is then converted to a corner point by using \<emph\>Corner Point\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153838				0	hi	\<image id=\"img_id3146969\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezierinsert.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3146969\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153710				0	hi	Insert Points				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149020				0	hi	Delete Points				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148917				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierDelete\"\>Use the \<emph\>Delete Points\</emph\> icon to delete one or several selected points. If you wish to select several points click the appropriate points while holding down the Shift key.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153766				0	hi	जिन बिन्दुओं को मिटाना है, पहले उन्हें चुनें, फिर इस प्रतीक को क्लिक करें या डिलीट बटन दबाएँ.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3147321				0	hi	\<image id=\"img_id3146920\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezierdelete.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3146920\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3155961				0	hi	Delete Points				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147361				0	hi	Split Curve				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3151248				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierCutLine\"\>The\<emph\> Split Curve \</emph\>icon splits a curve. Select the point or points where you want to split the curve, then click the icon\</ahelp\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153788				0	hi	\<image id=\"img_id3148489\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziercutline.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148489\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3152581				0	hi	Split Curve				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150345				0	hi	Convert To Curve				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148420				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierConvert\"\>Converts a curve into a straight line or converts a straight line into a curve.\</ahelp\> If you select a single point, the curve before the point will be converted. If two points are selected, the curve between both points will be converted. If you select more than two points, each time you click this icon, a different portion of the curve will be converted. If necessary, round points are converted into corner points and corner points are converted into round points.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	hi	यदि किसी वक्र का कोई खण्ड सीधा होता है, तो लकीर के अंत बिन्दु में प्रत्येक में अधिकतम एक नियंत्रण बिन्दु होते हैं. उन्हें गोल बिन्दु में परिवर्धित नहीं किया जा सकता जब तक कि सीधी लकीर को वापस वक्र में बदल नहीं लिया जाता.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3158212				0	hi	\<image id=\"img_id3149036\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezierconvert.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149036\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3158445				0	hi	Convert To Curve				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153199				0	hi	Corner Point				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148460				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierEdge\"\>Converts the selected point or points into corner points.\</ahelp\> Corner points have two movable control points, which are independent from each other. A curved line, therefore, does not go straight through a corner point, but forms a corner.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3154576				0	hi	\<image id=\"img_id3154201\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezieredge.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154201\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3166429				0	hi	Corner Point				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166436				0	hi	Smooth Transition				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3155510				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierSmooth\"\>Converts a corner point or symmetrical point into a smooth point.\</ahelp\> Both control points of the corner point are aligned in parallel, and can only be moved simultaneously. The control points may differentiate in length, allowing you to vary the degree of curvature.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3148813				0	hi	\<image id=\"img_id3151183\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziersmooth.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151183\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	hi	Smooth Transition				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159622				0	hi	Symmetric Transition				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3155812				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierSymmetric\"\>This icon converts a corner point or a smooth point into a symmetrical point.\</ahelp\> Both control points of the corner point are aligned in parallel and have the same length. They can only be moved simultaneously and the degree of curvature is the same in both directions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	hi	\<image id=\"img_id3159218\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_beziersymmetric.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159218\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3146866				0	hi	Symmetric Transition				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146786				0	hi	Close Bézier				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierClose\"\>Closes a line or a curve.\</ahelp\> A line is closed by connecting the last point with the first point, indicated by an enlarged square.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0227.xhp	0	help	par_id3154344				0	hi	\<image id=\"img_id3148607\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezierclose.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148607\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
