helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0213.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157896				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>Toolbars; Form Navigation bar\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Navigation bar; forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sorting; data in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; sorting in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms; sorting data\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0213.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157896				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigation Bar\"\>Form Navigation Bar\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0213.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	hi	The \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> bar contains icons to edit a database table or to control the data view. The bar is displayed at the bottom of a document that contains fields that are linked to a database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0213.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958				0	hi	You can use the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> bar to move within records as well as to insert and to delete records. If data is saved in a form, the changes are transferred to the database. The \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> bar also contains sort, filter, and search functions for data records.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0213.xhp	0	help	par_idN10717				0	hi	You can use the Navigation bar icon on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\"\>More Controls \</link\> bar to add a Navigation bar to a form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0213.xhp	0	help	par_id3157910				0	hi	The Navigation bar is only visible for forms connected to a database. In the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/04030000.xhp\" name=\"Design view\"\>Design view\</link\> of a form, the Navigation bar is not available. See also \<link href=\"text/shared/main0212.xhp\" name=\"Database Bar\"\>Table Data bar\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0213.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	hi	आप डाटा के दृश्य को छांटने व फ़िल्टर करने के फंक्शन के जरिए नियंत्रित कर सकते हैं. मूल तालिकाएँ परिवर्तित नहीं होंगी.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0213.xhp	0	help	par_id3153062				0	hi	The current sort order or filter is saved with the current document. If a filter is set, the \<emph\>Apply Filter\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> bar is activated. Sorting and filtering features in the document can also be configured in the \<emph\>Form Properties\</emph\> dialog. (Choose \<emph\>Form Properties - Data\</emph\> - properties \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"Sort\"\>\<emph\>Sort\</emph\>\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"Filter\"\>\<emph\>Filter\</emph\>\</link\>).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0213.xhp	0	help	par_id3149810				0	hi	If an SQL statement is the basis for a form (see \<emph\>Form Properties\</emph\> - tab \<emph\>Data\</emph\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"Data Source\"\>\<emph\>Data Source\</emph\>\</link\>), then the filter and sort functions are only available when the SQL statement refers to only one table and is not written in the native SQL mode.				20200411 15:09:53
