helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	hi	$[officename] बेसिक में प्रोसीजर तथा फ़ंक्शन का इस्तेमाल निम्न अनुसार वर्णित है:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	hi	$[officename] Basic provides tools to help you structuring your projects. It supports various "units" which enable you to group individual SUBS and FUNCTIONS in a Basic project.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148575				0	hi	लाइब्रेरीज़				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011				0	hi	Libraries serve as a tool for organizing modules, and can either be attached to a document or a template. When the document or a template is saved, all modules contained in the library are automatically saved as well.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112				0	hi	लाइब्रेरी में 16000 मॉड्यूल हो सकते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149262				0	hi	मॉडयूल				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	hi	A module contains SUBS and FUNCTIONS along with variable declarations. The length of the program that can be saved in a module is limited to 64 KB. If more space is required you can divide a $[officename] Basic project among several modules, and then save them in a single library.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152577				0	hi	संवाद मॉड्यूल्स				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020500.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	hi	Dialog modules contain dialog definitions, including the dialog box properties, the properties of each dialog element and the events assigned. Since a dialog module can only contain a single dialog, they are often referred to as "dialogs".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000003.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	Information				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148550				0	hi	Information				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_id3153381				0	hi	You can set the locale used for controlling the formatting numbers, dates and currencies in $[officename] Basic in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</emph\>. In Basic format codes, the decimal point (\<emph\>.\</emph\>) is always used as \<emph\>placeholder\</emph\> for the decimal separator defined in your locale and will be replaced by the corresponding character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	hi	The same applies to the locale settings for date, time and currency formats. The Basic format code will be interpreted and displayed according to your locale setting.				20200411 15:09:53
