helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150616				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03080101.xhp\" name=\"Atn Function [Runtime]\"\>Atn Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	hi	Trigonometric function that returns the arctangent of a numeric expression. The return value is in the range -Pi/2 to +Pi/2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	hi	The arctangent is the inverse of the tangent function. The Atn Function returns the angle "Alpha", expressed in radians, using the tangent of this angle. The function can also return the angle "Alpha" by comparing the ratio of the length of the side that is opposite of the angle to the length of the side that is adjacent to the angle in a right-angled triangle.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	hi	Atn(side opposite the angle/side adjacent to angle)= Alpha				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149669				0	hi	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148947				0	hi	Sin (Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148664				0	hi	वापसी मूल्य:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150359				0	hi	Double				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148798				0	hi	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3156212				0	hi	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Any numerical expression that represents the ratio of two sides of a right triangle. The Atn function returns the corresponding angle in radians (arctangent).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	hi	रेडियन से डिग्री में बदलने के लिए, रेडियन को 180/pi से गुणा करें.				20200411 15:09:53
