helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149670				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>TimeValue function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149670				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030206.xhp\" name=\"TimeValue Function [Runtime]\"\>TimeValue Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361				0	hi	Calculates a serial time value from the specified hour, minute, and second - parameters passed as strings - that represents the time in a single numeric value. This value can be used to calculate the difference between times.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154138				0	hi	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3156282				0	hi	TimeValue (Text As String)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153969				0	hi	वापसी मूल्य:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	hi	Date				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145172				0	hi	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	hi	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> Any string expression that contains the time that you want to calculate in the format "HH:MM:SS".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578				0	hi	Use the TimeValue function to convert any time into a single value, so that you can calculate time differences.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	hi	This TimeValue function returns the type Variant with VarType 7 (Date), and stores this value internally as a double-precision number between 0 and 0.9999999999.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3151117				0	hi	As opposed to the DateSerial or the DateValue function, where serial date values result in days relative to a fixed date, you can calculate with the values that are returned by the TimeValue function, but you cannot evaluate them.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426				0	hi	In the TimeSerial function, you can pass individual parameters (hour, minute, second) as separate numeric expressions. For the TimeValue function, however, you can pass a string as a parameter containing the time.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145271				0	hi	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3152597				0	hi	Sub ExampleTimerValue				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3147348				0	hi	Dim daDT as Date				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	hi	Dim a1, b1, c1, a2, b2, c2 as String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3149378				0	hi	a1 = "start time"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3145800				0	hi	b1 = "end time"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3151074				0	hi	c1 = "total time"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3154492				0	hi	a2 = "8:34"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	hi	b2 = "18:12"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	hi	daDT = TimeValue(b2) - TimeValue(a2)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3153838				0	hi	c2 = a1 & ": " & a2 & chr(13)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	hi	c2 = c2 & b1 & ": " & b2 & chr(13)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030206.xhp	0	help	par_id3154755				0	hi	c2 = c2 & c1 & ": " & trim(Str(Hour(daDT))) & ":" & trim(Str(Minute(daDT))) & ":" & trim(Str(Second(daDT)))				20200411 15:09:53
