helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030103.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423				0	hi	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> A numeric expression that contains a serial date number from which you can determine the day of the month.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	hi	This function is basically the opposite of the DateSerial function, returning the day of the month from a serial date number generated by the \<emph\>DateSerial\</emph\> or the \<emph\>DateValue\</emph\> function. For example, the expression				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364				0	hi	Print Day (DateSerial(1994, 12, 20))				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153190				0	hi	returns the value 20.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149481				0	hi	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155413				0	hi	sub ExampleDay				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	hi	Print "Day " & Day(DateSerial(1994, 12, 20)) & " of the month"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	hi	end sub				20200411 15:09:53
