helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150502				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030000.xhp\" name=\"Date and Time Functions\"\>Date and Time Functions\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153255				0	hi	Use the statements and functions described here to perform date and time calculations.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152363				0	hi	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Basic lets you calculate time or date differences by converting the time and date values to continuous numeric values. After the difference is calculated, special functions are used to reconvert the values to the standard time or date formats.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	hi	You can combine date and time values into a single floating-decimal number. Dates are converted to integers, and times to decimal values. \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Basic also supports the variable type Date, which can contain a time specification consisting of both a date and time.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	Open Statement [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
