helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156215				0	hi	Boolean expressions combined with AND only return the value \<emph\>True\</emph\> if both expressions evaluate to \<emph\>True\</emph\>:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	hi	\<emph\>True\</emph\> AND \<emph\>True\</emph\> returns \<emph\>True\</emph\>; for all other combinations the result is \<emph\>False\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	hi	The AND operator also performs a bitwise comparison of identically positioned bits in two numeric expressions.				20200411 15:09:53
