helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	hi	Number,Mine=12				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149256				0	hi	वैध नहीं, विरामचिह्न स्वीकार्य नहीं हैं				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146317				0	hi	वेरिएबल्स डिक्लेयर करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150299	18			0	hi	In $[officename] Basic you don't need to declare variables explicitly. A variable declaration can be performed with the \<emph\>Dim\</emph\> statement. You can declare more than one variable at a time by separating the names with a comma. To define the variable type, use either a type-declaration sign after the name, or the appropriate key word. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154118				0	hi	वेरिएबल डिक्लेरेशन के लिए उदाहरण:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090				0	hi	DIM a$				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150982				0	hi	Declares the variable "a" as a String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149531				0	hi	DIM a As String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150343				0	hi	Declares the variable "a" as a String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149036				0	hi	DIM a$, b As Integer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155507				0	hi	वेरिएबल को स्ट्रिंग के रूप में तथा एक को पूर्णांक के रूप में डिक्लेयर करता है				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10854				0	hi	DIM c As Boolean				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10859				0	hi	c को बूलिए वेरिएबल के रूप में डिक्लेयर करता है जो TRUE या FALSE हो सकता है				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150519				0	hi	It is very important when declaring variables that you use the type-declaration character each time, even if it was used in the declaration instead of a keyword. Thus the following statements are invalid:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	hi	DIM a$				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154527				0	hi	"a" को स्ट्रिंग के रुप में डिक्लेयर करता है				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148599				0	hi	a="TestString"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153064				0	hi	टाइप डिक्लेरेशन गुम है: "a$="				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3144770				0	hi	Once you have declared a variable as a certain type, you cannot declare the variable under the same name again as a different type!				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149331				0	hi	वेरिएबल डिक्लेरेशन फ़ोर्स करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149443				0	hi	वेरिएबल का डिक्लेरेशन फोर्स करने के लिए, निम्न कमांड का इस्तेमाल करें:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	hi	OPTION EXPLICIT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155072				0	hi	The \<emph\>Option Explicit\</emph\> statement has to be the first line in the module, before the first SUB. Generally, only arrays need to be declared explicitly. All other variables are declared according to the type-declaration character, or - if omitted - as the default type \<emph\>Single\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154614				0	hi	वेरिएबल क़िस्में				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155383				0	hi	$[officename] बेसिक चार वेरिएबल क्लास को समर्थित करता है:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153972	36			0	hi	\<emph\>Numeric\</emph\> variables can contain number values. Some variables are used to store large or small numbers, and others are used for floating-point or fractional numbers. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159226				0	hi	\<emph\>String\</emph\> variables contain character strings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145217				0	hi	\<emph\>Boolean\</emph\> variables contain either the TRUE or the FALSE value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762				0	hi	\<emph\>Object\</emph\> variables can store objects of various types, like tables and documents within a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153805				0	hi	पूर्णांक वेरिएबल्स				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146966				0	hi	Integer variables range from -32768 to 32767. If you assign a floating-point value to an integer variable, the decimal places are rounded to the next integer. Integer variables are rapidly calculated in procedures and are suitable for counter variables in loops. An integer variable only requires two bytes of memory. "%" is the type-declaration character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810				0	hi	Dim Variable%				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153556				0	hi	Dim Variable As Integer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147546				0	hi	Long Integer Variables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151193				0	hi	Long integer variables range from -2147483648 to 2147483647. If you assign a floating-point value to a long integer variable, the decimal places are rounded to the next integer. Long integer variables are rapidly calculated in procedures and are suitable for counter variables in loops for large values. A long integer variable requires four bytes of memory. "&" is the type-declaration character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154708				0	hi	Dim Variable&				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156365				0	hi	Dim Variable as Long				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id7596972				0	hi	Decimal Variables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id2649311				0	hi	Decimal variables can take positive or negative numbers or zero. Accuracy is up to 29 digits.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id7617114				0	hi	You can use plus (+) or minus (-) signs as prefixes for decimal numbers (with or without spaces).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id1593676				0	hi	If a decimal number is assigned to an integer variable, %PRODUCTNAME Basic rounds the figure up or down.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147500				0	hi	एकल वेरिएबल्स				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153070				0	hi	Single variables can take positive or negative values ranging from 3.402823 x 10E38 to 1.401298 x 10E-45. Single variables are floating-point variables, in which the decimal precision decreases as the non-decimal part of the number increases. Single variables are suitable for mathematical calculations of average precision. Calculations require more time than for Integer variables, but are faster than calculations with Double variables. A Single variable requires 4 bytes of memory. The type-declaration character is "!".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149875				0	hi	Dim Variable!				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153302				0	hi	Dim Variable as Single				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155753				0	hi	दोहरे वेरिएबल्स				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150953				0	hi	Double variables can take positive or negative values ranging from 1.79769313486232 x 10E308 to 4.94065645841247 x 10E-324. Double variables are floating-point variables, in which the decimal precision decreases as the non-decimal part of the number increases. Double variables are suitable for precise calculations. Calculations require more time than for Single variables. A Double variable requires 8 bytes of memory. The type-declaration character is "#".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150431				0	hi	Dim Variable#				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154406				0	hi	Dim Variable As Double				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155747				0	hi	करंसी वेरिएबल्स				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153337				0	hi	Currency variables are internally stored as 64-bit numbers (8 Bytes) and displayed as a fixed-decimal number with 15 non-decimal and 4 decimal places. The values range from -922337203685477.5808 to +922337203685477.5807. Currency variables are used to calculate currency values with a high precision. The type-declaration character is "@".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147296				0	hi	Dim Variable@				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	hi	Dim Variable As Currency				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148742				0	hi	वाक्यांश वेरिएबल्स				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151393				0	hi	String variables can hold character strings with up to 65,535 characters. Each character is stored as the corresponding Unicode value. String variables are suitable for word processing within programs and for temporary storage of any non-printable character up to a maximum length of 64 Kbytes. The memory required for storing string variables depends on the number of characters in the variable. The type-declaration character is "$".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3166467				0	hi	Dim Variable$				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153027				0	hi	Dim Variable As String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150534				0	hi	बूलिये वेरिएबल्स				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145632				0	hi	Boolean variables store only one of two values: TRUE or FALSE. A number 0 evaluates to FALSE, every other value evaluates to TRUE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147615				0	hi	Dim Variable As Boolean				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149722				0	hi	तारीख़ वेरिएबल्स				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159116				0	hi	Date variables can only contain dates and time values stored in an internal format. Values assigned to Date variables with \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030101.xhp\" name=\"Dateserial\"\>\<emph\>Dateserial\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030102.xhp\" name=\"Datevalue\"\>\<emph\>Datevalue\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030205.xhp\" name=\"Timeserial\"\>\<emph\>Timeserial\</emph\>\</link\> or \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030206.xhp\" name=\"Timevalue\"\>\<emph\>Timevalue\</emph\>\</link\> are automatically converted to the internal format. Date-variables are converted to normal numbers by using the \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030103.xhp\" name=\"Day\"\>\<emph\>Day\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030104.xhp\" name=\"Month\"\>\<emph\>Month\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030106.xhp\" name=\"Year\"\>\<emph\>Year\</emph\>\</link\> or the \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030201.xhp\" name=\"Hour\"\>\<emph\>Hour\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030202.xhp\" name=\"Minute\"\>\<emph\>Minute\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030204.xhp\" name=\"Second\"\>\<emph\>Second\</emph\>\</link\> function. The internal format enables a comparison of date/time values by calculating the difference between two numbers. These variables can only be declared with the key word \<emph\>Date\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150462				0	hi	Dim Variable As Date				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148732				0	hi	Initial Variable Values				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154549				0	hi	As soon as the variable has been declared, it is automatically set to the "Null" value. Note the following conventions:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3143222				0	hi	\<emph\>Numeric\</emph\> variables are automatically assigned the value "0" as soon as they are declared.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150693				0	hi	\<emph\>Date variables\</emph\> are assigned the value 0 internally; equivalent to converting the value to "0" with the \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030103.xhp\" name=\"Day\"\>\<emph\>Day\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030104.xhp\" name=\"Month\"\>\<emph\>Month\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030106.xhp\" name=\"Year\"\>\<emph\>Year\</emph\>\</link\> or the \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030201.xhp\" name=\"Hour\"\>\<emph\>Hour\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030202.xhp\" name=\"Minute\"\>\<emph\>Minute\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030204.xhp\" name=\"Second\"\>\<emph\>Second\</emph\>\</link\> function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154807				0	hi	\<emph\>String variables\</emph\> are assigned an empty-string ("") when they are declared.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153936				0	hi	Arrays				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148736				0	hi	$[officename] Basic knows one- or multi-dimensional arrays, defined by a specified variable type. Arrays are suitable for editing lists and tables in programs. Individual elements of an array can be addressed through a numeric index.				20200411 15:09:53
