helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\control_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3147317				0	hi	You can set the properties of control that you add to a dialog. For example, you can change the color, name, and size of a button that you added. You can change most control properties when you create or edit a dialog. However, you can only change some properties at runtime.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\guide\control_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3145749				0	hi	To change the properties of a control in design mode, right-click the control, and then choose \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
