helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149664				0	hi	Apply field format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_FORMATTER\"\>Specifies that all field formats are considered when searching in the current document.\</ahelp\> Field formats are all visible formats that are created using the following possibilities:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	hi	in table design mode for field properties,				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150488				0	hi	in data source view on column formatting,				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152941				0	hi	in forms on control properties.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156736				0	hi	If the \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> box is marked, the data source view of the table or form is searched using the formatting set there. If the box is not marked, the database is searched using the formatting saved in the database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151280				0	hi	उदाहरण:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	hi	You have a date field, which is saved in "DD.MM.YY" format in the database (for example, 17.02.65). The format of the entry is changed in the data source view to "DD MMM YYYY" (17 Feb 1965). Following this example, a record containing February 17 is only found when the \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> option is on:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150593				0	hi	Apply field format				20200411 15:09:53
