helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148765				0	hi	Cut				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	par_id3153383				0	hi	Cuts out the selected object and stores it on the clipboard. The object can be reinserted from the clipboard by using \<emph\>Paste\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156069				0	hi	Paste				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	par_id3154896				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_EXPLORERCONTENT_PASTE\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Inserts the element that you moved to the clipboard into the document.\</ahelp\> This command can only be called if the contents of the clipboard can be inserted at the current cursor position.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149948				0	hi	प्रविष्ट				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	par_id3147588				0	hi	Opens a submenu in the Gallery where you can choose between \<emph\>Copy\</emph\> and \<emph\>Link\</emph\>. The selected Gallery object is either copied into the current document or a link is created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	par_id3146130				0	hi	If you have selected an object in your document, then a new insertion will replace the selected object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145829				0	hi	पृष्ठ भूमि				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	par_id3149180				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_GALLERY_MN_BACKGROUND\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Inserts the selected picture as a background graphic.\</ahelp\> Use the submenu commands \<emph\>Page\</emph\> or \<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\> to define whether the graphic should cover the entire page or only the current paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153049				0	hi	Copy				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_EXPLORERCONTENT_COPY\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Copies the selected element to the clipboard.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148620				0	hi	Delete				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	par_id3154317				0	hi	\<ahelp visibility=\"visible\" hid=\"SID_EXPLORERCONTENT_DESTROY\"\>Deletes the current selection. If multiple objects are selected, all will be deleted. In most cases, a \<link href=\"text/shared/01/03150100.xhp\" name=\"security query\"\>security query\</link\> appears before objects are deleted.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	par_id3155941				0	hi	The object is either physically deleted from the data carrier or the object display is removed, depending on context.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	par_id3150506				0	hi	If you choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> while in the Gallery, the entry will be deleted from the Gallery, but the file itself will remain untouched.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150443				0	hi	खोलें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	par_id3149149	137			0	hi	\<ahelp visibility=\"visible\" hid=\"SID_EXPLORERCONTENT_OPEN_OBJECT\"\>Use the\<emph\> Open \</emph\>command to open the selected object in a new task.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149732				0	hi	नाम बदलें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	par_id3149797				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_EXPLORERCONTENT_RENAME\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Enables a selected object to be renamed.\</ahelp\> After selecting \<emph\>Rename\</emph\> the name is selected and a new one can be entered directly. Use the arrow keys to set the cursor at the beginning or end of the name to delete or add to part of the name or to reposition the cursor.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155434				0	hi	अद्यतन				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	par_id3154898				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_GALLERY_ACTUALIZE\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Updates the view in the window or in the selected object.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147573				0	hi	Preview				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	par_id3155583				0	hi	The element selected is displayed in the Gallery at maximum size. Double-click the preview to switch back to the normal Gallery view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157809				0	hi	कड़ी तैयार करें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000010.xhp	0	help	par_id3153716				0	hi	This command can be activated if an object is selected. A link named "Link to xxx" (\<emph\>xxx\</emph\> represents the name of the object) will be created directly in the same directory as that of the selected object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	Frequently-Used Buttons				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152952				0	hi	Frequently-Used Buttons				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147617				0	hi	Cancel				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155913				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Clicking \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\> closes a dialog without saving any changes made.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id2341685				0	hi	Finish				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id6909390				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Applies all changes and closes the wizard.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147477				0	hi	Toolbars				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149783				0	hi	By clicking the arrow next to some icons you open a toolbar. To move a toolbar, drag the title bar. As soon as you release the mouse button, the toolbar remains at the new position. Drag the title bar to another position, or drag to an edge of the window, where the toolbar will dock. Close a toolbar by clicking the Close Window icon. Make the toolbar visible again by choosing \<emph\>View - Toolbars - (toolbar name)\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152414				0	hi	Spin button				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id1094088				0	hi	In form controls, a spin button is a property of a numerical field, currency field, date field, or time field. If the property "Spin button" is enabled, the field shows a pair of symbols with arrows pointing to opposing directions, either vertically or horizontally.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id7493209				0	hi	In the Basic IDE, a spin button is the name used for the numerical field together with the two arrow symbols.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155599				0	hi	You can type a numerical value into the field next to the spin button, or select the value with the up-arrow or down-arrow symbols on the spin button. On the keyboard you can press the up arrow and down arrow keys to increase or reduce the value. You can press the Page Up and Page Down keys to set the maximum and minimum value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150264				0	hi	If the field next to the spin button defines numerical values, you can also define a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000003.xhp#metrik\" name=\"measurement unit\"\>measurement unit\</link\>, for example, 1 cm or 5 mm, 12 pt or 2".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154232				0	hi	बदलें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148983				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you click forward through the dialog, this button is called \<emph\>Next\</emph\>. On the last page the button has the name \<emph\>Convert\</emph\>. The conversion is then performed by clicking the button.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145129				0	hi	Context Menu				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156553				0	hi	\<variable id=\"context\"\>To activate the context menu of an object, first click the object with the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>left\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> mouse button to select it, and then, \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>while holding down the Ctrl key or the Command and Option keys, click the mouse button again\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\> click the right mouse button\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>. Some context menus can be called even if the object has not been selected. Context menus are found just about everywhere in $[officename].\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149180				0	hi	Delete				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Deletes the selected element or elements after confirmation.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147557				0	hi	Delete				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Deletes the selected element or elements without requiring confirmation.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148620				0	hi	Metrics				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	hi	You can enter values in the input fields in different units of measurement. The default unit is inches. However, if you want a space of exactly 1cm, then type "1cm". Additional units are available according to the context, for example, 12 pt for a 12 point spacing. If the value of the new unit is unrealistic, the program uses a predefined maximum or minimum value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155535				0	hi	Close				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Closes the dialog and saves all changes.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275				0	hi	Close				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Closes the dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
