helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3149767				0	hi	If you selected one of the date formats (DMY), (MDY), or (YMD) and you enter numbers without date delimiters, the numbers are interpreted as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3150650	76			0	hi	अक्षरों की संख्या				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3150495				0	hi	तारीख़ फार्मेट				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3156212				0	hi	6				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3153056				0	hi	Two characters each are taken for day, month, and year in the selected order.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3147352				0	hi	8				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	hi	Four characters are taken for the year, two each for month and day, in the selected order.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295				0	hi	5 or 7				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3151168				0	hi	As with 6 or 8 characters, but the first part of the sequence has one character less. This will suppress a leading zero for month and day.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143				0	hi	If you want to include the leading zero in the data you import, in telephone numbers for example, apply the "Text" format to the column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149287				0	hi	Preview				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3147377				0	hi	Shows how the imported text will look after it is separated into columns. To apply a format to a column when it is imported, click a column and select a \<emph\>Column type\</emph\>. When you select a \<emph\>Column type\</emph\>, the column heading displays the applied format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000208.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	hi	If you want to use a fixed width to separate the imported data into columns, click in the ruler to set the width boundaries.				20200411 15:09:53
