helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156410				0	hi	Starting the $[officename] Software With Parameters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147009				0	hi	By starting the $[officename] software from the command line you can assign various parameters, with which you can influence the performance. The use of command line parameters is only recommended for experienced users.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	hi	For normal handling, the use of command line parameters is not necessary. A few of the parameters require a deeper knowledge of the technical background of the $[officename] software technology.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154898				0	hi	कमांड लाइन से $[officename] सॉफ़्टवेयर को प्रारंभ करना 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3156152				0	hi	Under Windows, select \<emph\>Run\</emph\> from the Windows Start menu, or open a Shell under UNIX® based platforms.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472	6			0	hi	Under Windows, type the following text in the \<emph\>Open \</emph\>text field and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669				0	hi	Under UNIX based systems, type the following line of text, then press \<emph\>Return\</emph\>:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147561	7			0	hi	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>{install}\\program\\soffice.exe {parameter} \</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>{install}/program/soffice {parameter} \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	hi	Replace \<emph\>{install}\</emph\> with the path to your installation of the $[officename] software (for example, \<emph\>C:\\Program Files\\Office\</emph\>, or \<emph\>~/office\</emph\>)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3158407				0	hi	Where required, replace \<emph\>{parameter}\</emph\> with one or more of the following command line parameters.				20200411 15:09:53
