helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	hi	चेकबॉक्स, बटन, डाटा रेकॉर्ड दिखाती तालिकाएँ तथा दस्तावेज़ के अन्य नियंत्रक को जोड़ने के लिए आप फ़ॉर्म नियंत्रक औजारपट्टी का इस्तेमाल कर सकते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077F				0	hi	दस्तावेज़ में बटन जोड़ने के लिए				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	hi	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars - Form Controls\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	hi	On the Form Controls toolbar, click the \<emph\>Push Button\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A4				0	hi	माउस संकेतक धन-चिह्न जैसा बदल जाएगा.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	hi	दस्तावेज़ में बटन बनाने के लिए माउस संकेतक को खींचें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	hi	Right-click the button and choose \<emph\>Control\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CD				0	hi	बटन के गुणों को निर्धारित करें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154923				0	hi	To change the button label, click the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab, and edit the text in the \<emph\>Label\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303	12			0	hi	To attach a macro to the button, click the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab, and click the \<emph\>... \</emph\>button beside the button action that you want to run the macro. In the \<emph\>Assign Macro\</emph\> dialog, locate the macro that you want to use, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10814				0	hi	Close the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147350				0	hi	(वैकल्पिक) बटन से सम्बन्धित फ़ॉर्म के गुणों को निर्धारित करें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10828				0	hi	Right-click the button and choose \<emph\>Form\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	hi	The \<emph\>Form Properties\</emph\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	hi	फ़ॉर्म के लिए गुणों को निर्धारित करता है तथा संवाद को बन्द करता है.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	तालिका तथा तालिका कक्षों के लिए किनारा निर्धारित करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155805				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>tables in text; defining borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables in spreadsheets;defining borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders; for tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; around tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;table borders\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155805				0	hi	\<variable id=\"border_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/border_table.xhp\" name=\"Defining Borders for Tables and Table Cells\"\>Defining Borders for Tables and Table Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147008				0	hi	Setting a Predefined Border Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	hi	Select the table cells that you want to modify.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346	3			0	hi	Click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Table \</emph\>toolbar (Writer) or on the \<emph\>Line and Filling\</emph\> bar to open the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270				0	hi	किसी एक पूर्वनिर्धारित किनारा शैली में क्लिक करें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156156				0	hi	This \<emph\>adds\</emph\> the selected style to the current border style of the table cells. Select the blank border style at the top left of the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window to clear all border styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153666				0	hi	Setting a Customized Border Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	hi	Select the table cells that you want to modify.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Table - Table Properties - Borders\</emph\> (Writer) or \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\> (Calc).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	hi	In the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area select the edge(s) that you want to appear in a common layout. Click on an edge in the preview to toggle the selection of an edge.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id31594132				0	hi	If you select more than one row or column, you can change the middle lines between rows or columns. Select the middle markers in the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526				0	hi	Select a line style and color for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145606				0	hi	Repeat the last two steps for every border edge.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	hi	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149807				0	hi	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	Opening a Document Using WebDAV over HTTPS				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	bm_id7430951				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>opening;documents on WebDAV server\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>WebDAV over HTTPS\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>digital signatures;WebDAV over HTTPS\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	hd_id4989165				0	hi	\<variable id=\"digitalsign_receive\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digitalsign_receive.xhp\"\>Opening a Document Using WebDAV over HTTPS\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1399578				0	hi	In %PRODUCTNAME, you can open and save documents that are stored on a WebDAV server, using the secure HTTPS protocol.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id598162				0	hi	You must use the %PRODUCTNAME file dialogs to use WebDAV over HTTPS.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id7309793				0	hi	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - General\</item\>. Ensure that \<emph\>Use %PRODUCTNAME dialogs\</emph\> is enabled. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialog box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1227759				0	hi	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id7424237				0	hi	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, enter the path to the WebDAV folder. For example, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>https://192.168.1.1/webfolder\</item\> to open a secure connection to the WebDAV server at the IP address 192.168.1.1, and to list the contents of the \<item type=\"literal\"\>webfolder\</item\> folder.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1388592				0	hi	The first time you connect to a WebDAV server, you see the "\<emph\>Website Certified by an Unknown Authority\</emph\>" dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id343943				0	hi	You should click the \<emph\>Examine Certificate\</emph\> button and examine the certificate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id8726767				0	hi	If you accept the certificate, choose "\<emph\>Accept this certificate temporarily for this session\</emph\>" and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. Now you can open and save files from the WebDAV server without further questions, until you exit %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id691549				0	hi	If you do not trust the certificate, click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	hi	If you did accept the certificate, you can now select the file name or file names you want to open and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3236182				0	hi	If there is a mismatch of the domain name given in the certificate and the domain name you entered in the file dialog, then you see a dialog that allows you to choose from any of the following options:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1251258				0	hi	 \<emph\>View Certificate\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the View Certificate dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id8111819				0	hi	 \<emph\>Continue\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you are sure both domains are the same, click the Continue button.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id9116794				0	hi	 \<emph\>Cancel Connection\</emph\> - Cancels the connection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id4381847				0	hi	If you click \<emph\>Continue\</emph\>, you may see a dialog that asks you to enter your user name and password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1336710				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter your user name to log on to the WebDAV server.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
