helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3149797	6			0	hi	If the \<emph\>Always create backup copy\</emph\> option is selected, the old version of the file is saved to the backup directory whenever you save the current version of the file. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	hi	You can change the backup directory by choosing \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Paths\</emph\>, then change the \<emph\>Backups\</emph\> path in the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3149415				0	hi	The backup copy has the same name as the document, but the extension is .BAK. If the backup folder already contains such a file, it will be overwritten without warning.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149514				0	hi	प्रत्येक n मिनटों में रिकवरी जानकारी स्वचालित रुप से सहेजने के लिए				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010200.xhp\" name=\"Load/Save - General\"\>Load/Save - General\</link\>\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	hi	Mark \<emph\>Save AutoRecovery information every\</emph\> and select the time interval.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_autosave.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526				0	hi	This command saves the information necessary to restore the current document in case of a crash. Additionally, in case of a crash %PRODUCTNAME tries automatically to save AutoRecovery information for all open documents, if possible.				20200411 15:09:53
