helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator_setcursor.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	hi	You can use the \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> toolbar to scroll to the previous or next object of a specific category.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator_setcursor.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	hi	Open the toolbar using the \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> icon below the vertical scroll bar of a text document, or in the Navigator window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator_setcursor.xhp	0	help	par_id3153348				0	hi	On the \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> toolbar, you first select the category, then click on one of the buttons, \<emph\>Previous Object\</emph\> or \<emph\>Next Object\</emph\>. The names of the buttons refer to the category, for example, the button "Next Object" is named "Next Page" or "Next Bookmark" according to the category.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	विशिष्ट अक्षर प्रविष्ट करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>characters; special\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; special characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>special characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; inserting special characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>accents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>compose key to insert special characters\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927				0	hi	\<variable id=\"insert_specialchar\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_specialchar.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Special Characters\"\>Inserting Special Characters\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	hi	This function allows you to insert special characters, such as check marks, boxes, and telephone symbols, into your text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	hi	To view a selection of all characters, choose \<emph\>Insert - Special Character\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	hi	In the large selection field click the desired character or several characters in succession. The characters are displayed at the bottom of the dialog. When you close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>, all displayed characters in the selected font are inserted in the current document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	hi	In any text input field (such as the input fields in the \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialog) you can press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+S to open the \<emph\>Special Characters\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3155630				0	hi	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>At present there are three ways of entering letters with accents directly from the keyboard.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897				0	hi	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>\<emph\>Solaris:\</emph\> Using a Sun keyboard. First press the Compose key to the right of the space bar, then enter the first and second modifiers.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	hi	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>\<emph\>Linux / NetBSD:\</emph\> Using the dead-keys. In an xterm window first press the (´) or (`) key. The character should not appear on the screen. Now press a letter, such as "e". The e is given an accent, é or è. If not, then check in the XF86Config file if a "nodeadkeys" XkbdVariant has been loaded there and replace it. You may also have set the environment variable SAL_NO_DEADKEYS, which deactivates the dead-keys.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	hi	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>\<emph\>All Unix systems:\</emph\> (Alt Graph) as additional compose key. The (Alt Graph) key can work in $[officename] like the Compose key, if you set the environment variable SAL_ALTGR_COMPOSE. The (Alt Graph) key must trigger a mode_switch, so, for example, xmodmap -e "keysym Alt_R = Mode_switch" must be set. First press (Alt Graph), then the first modifier, then the second modifier. The characters are combined as described on a Solaris system in the file /usr/openwin/include/X11/Suncompose.h.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3149047				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04100000.xhp\" name=\"Special Characters\"\>Special Characters\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_specialchar.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"AutoCorrect\"\>AutoCorrect\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	स्वचालित यूआरएल पहचानना बन्द करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149346				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; URL recognition\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>recognizing URLs automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic hyperlink formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>URL;turning off URL recognition\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks;turning off automatic recognition\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>links;turning off automatic recognition\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>predictive text, see also AutoCorrect function/AutoFill function/AutoInput function/word completion/text completion\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346				0	hi	\<variable id=\"autocorr_url\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/autocorr_url.xhp\" name=\"Turning off Automatic URL Recognition\"\>Turning off Automatic URL Recognition\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	hi	When you enter text, $[officename] automatically recognizes a word that may be a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>URL\</link\> and replaces the word with a hyperlink. $[officename] formats the hyperlink with direct font attributes (color and underline) the properties of which are obtained from certain Character Styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561				0	hi	If you do not want $[officename] to automatically recognize URLs as you are typing, there are several ways of turning off this feature.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154306				0	hi	यूआरएल पहचानना पहले जैसा करें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	hi	When you are typing and notice that a text has just been automatically converted into a hyperlink, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z to undo this formatting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149235				0	hi	If you do not notice this conversion until later, select the hyperlink and choose the menu command \<emph\>Format - Default Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152350				0	hi	यूआरएल पहचानना बन्द करें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3149514				0	hi	उस क़िस्म का दस्तावेज़ लोड करें जिसके लिए आप यूआरएल पहचान को परिवर्धित करना चाहते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3151246				0	hi	यदि आप पाठ दस्तावेज़ों के लिए यूआरएल पहचान को परिवर्धित करना चाहते हैं तो, कोई पाठ दस्तावेज़ खोलें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	hi	In the \<emph\>AutoCorrect\</emph\> dialog, select the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	hi	If you unmark \<emph\>URL Recognition\</emph\>, words will no longer be automatically replaced with hyperlinks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autocorr_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423				0	hi	In $[officename] Writer there are two check boxes in front of \<emph\>URL Recognition\</emph\>. The box in the first column is for later post-editing and the box in the second column is for AutoCorrect as you type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	मापक इकाई चुनना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159201				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>documents;measurement units in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>measurement units;selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>units;measurement units\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>centimeters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inches\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>distances\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;measurement units\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159201				0	hi	\<variable id=\"measurement_units\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/measurement_units.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Measurement Units\"\>Selecting Measurement Units\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	hi	आप $[officename] राइटर, $[officename] राइटर/वेब, $[officename] कॅल्क, $[officename] इम्प्रेस तथा $[officename] ड्रा दस्तावेज़ों के लिए अलग मापक इकाइयाँ चुन सकते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_idN10674				0	hi	उस क़िस्म का दस्तावेज़ खोलें जिसके लिए आप मापक इकाई बदलना चाहते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	hi	संवाद के बाएँ फलक में, अनुप्रयोग को दोहरा क्लिक करें जिसके लिए आप मापक इकाई चुनना चाहते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3147653				0	hi	Double-click \<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer\</emph\> if you want to select the measurement units for text documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	hi	Click on \<emph\>General\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	hi	On the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab page, select the measurement unit. Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000003.xhp\" name=\"Entering measurement units directly\"\>Entering measurement units directly\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\measurement_units.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473				0	hi	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040200.xhp\" name=\"Writer - General\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - General\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	नया यूएनओ अवयव इंटीग्रेट करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149760				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>add-ons, see UNO components\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>UNO components;integrating new\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;UNO components\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149760				0	hi	\<variable id=\"integratinguno\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/integratinguno.xhp\" name=\"Integrating new UNO components\"\>Integrating new UNO components\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	hi	Programmers can write and integrate their own UNO (Universal Network Objects) components to $[officename]. Those new components can be added to the $[officename] menus and toolbars; we call them "Add-Ons".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	hi	The integration of new components is supported by some tools and services. Details can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide. The three main steps are as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748	3			0	hi	Register the new components within $[officename]. This can be accomplished using the tool \<item type=\"literal\"\>unopkg\</item\>, which can be found in {installpath}\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>/ \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\\\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>program.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	hi	Integrate the new components as services. The ProtocolHandler and JobDispatch services assist you; more information can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	hi	Change the user interface (menus or toolbars). This can be done almost automatically by writing an XML text file that describes the changes. More information can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110				0	hi	The Add-Ons can extend the functionality of $[officename]. They are not related to the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"Add-Ins\"\>Add-Ins\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Add-Ins\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> that provide new functions for $[officename] Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150620				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>protecting; contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>protected contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>contents protection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>encryption of contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>passwords for protecting contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>security;protecting contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>form controls; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>draw objects;protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>OLE objects;protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>graphics;protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames;protecting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	hi	\<variable id=\"protection\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/protection.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME\"\>Protecting Content in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	hi	The following is an overview of the different ways of protecting contents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> from being modified, deleted or viewed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	hi	जब सहेजा जाए तो सभी दस्तावेज़ों की सुरक्षा				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150775				0	hi	All documents that are saved in \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\" name=\"OpenDocument format\"\>OpenDocument format\</link\> can be saved with a password. Documents that are saved with a password cannot be opened without the password. The content is secured so that it cannot be read with an external editor. This applies to content, graphics and OLE objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	hi	Turning on protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145121				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> and mark the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> check box. Save the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154286				0	hi	Turning off protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148492				0	hi	Open the document, entering the correct password. Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068				0	hi	Information entered in \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\> is not encrypted. This includes the name of the author, creation date, word and character counts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149294				0	hi	रिवीजन मार्किंग की सुरक्षा				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3161646				0	hi	With every change made in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer, the review function records who made the change. This function can be turned on with protection, so that it can only be turned off when the correct password is entered. Until then, all changes will continue to be recorded. Acceptance or rejection of changes is not possible.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	hi	Turning on protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153104				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter and confirm a password of at least 5 characters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3144760				0	hi	Turning off protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152920				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter the correct password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155113				0	hi	फ्रेम, चित्र, तथा ओएलई वस्तुओं को सुरक्षित करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153703				0	hi	You can protect the content, position and size of inserted graphics. The same applies to frames (in Writer) and OLE objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147131				0	hi	Turning on protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	hi	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Picture - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, mark \<emph\>Contents\</emph\>, \<emph\>Position\</emph\> and/or \<emph\>Size\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147510				0	hi	Turning off protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153657				0	hi	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Picture - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, unmark as appropriate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152992				0	hi	फ़ॉर्म वस्तु तथा ड्राइंग वस्तु सुरक्षित करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166429	59			0	hi	The draw objects that you insert into your documents with the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>toolbar can be protected from being accidentally moved or changed in size. You can do the same with form objects inserted with the \<emph\>Form Controls\</emph\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153226				0	hi	Turning on protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148815	61			0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size \</emph\>- \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Mark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3156289				0	hi	Turning off protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154991	63			0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size \</emph\>- \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Unmark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B8C				0	hi	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp#digital_signatures\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
