helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	hi	उस दस्तावेज़ को खोलें जिसके लिए आप मॅक्रो रेकॉर्ड करना चाहते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Record Macro\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	hi	You see the small \<emph\>Recording\</emph\> dialog with just one button called \<emph\>Stop Recording\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087				0	hi	दस्तावेज़ में जिन्हें रेकॉर्ड करना हैं वे क्रियाएँ निष्पादित करें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504				0	hi	किसी वस्तु को अचयनित करने के लिए एस्केप कुंजी दबाएँ, चूंकि म्रॅक्रो रेकॉर्डर वर्तमान में इस क्रिया को माउस क्लिक से रेकॉर्ड नहीं कर रहा है.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3148492				0	hi	Click \<emph\>Stop Recording\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3148686				0	hi	The \<emph\>Macro\</emph\> dialog appears, in which you can save and run the macro.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3159158				0	hi	If you want to abort the recording without saving a macro, click the \<emph\>Close\</emph\> button of the \<emph\>Recording\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3144510				0	hi	To save the macro, first select the object where you want the macro to be saved in the \<emph\>Save macro in\</emph\> list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550	12			0	hi	If you want the macro to be saved into a new library or module, click the \<emph\>New Library \</emph\>or \<emph\>New Module \</emph\>button and enter a name for the library or module.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	hi	Enter a name for the new macro in the \<emph\>Macro name\</emph\> text box. Do not use Basic keywords as a name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	hi	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	hd_id2486342				0	hi	Limitations of the macro recorder				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3608508				0	hi	The following actions are \<emph\>not\</emph\> recorded:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id921353				0	hi	Opening of windows is not recorded.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id9296243				0	hi	Actions carried out in another window than where the recorder was started are not recorded.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id4269234				0	hi	Window switching is not recorded.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id8014465				0	hi	Actions that are not related to the document contents are not recorded. For example, changes made in the Options dialog, macro organizer, customizing.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id2814416				0	hi	Selections are recorded only if they are done by using the keyboard (cursor traveling), but not when the mouse is used.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id2522354				0	hi	The macro recorder works only in Calc and Writer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Macro\"\>Macro\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0600.xhp\" name=\"macro programming in $[officename]\"\>Programming in %PRODUCTNAME\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\macro_recording.xhp	0	help	par_id7797242				0	hi	The macro recording functionality is only available for text documents in %PRODUCTNAME Writer and for spreadsheets in %PRODUCTNAME Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	फ़ॉर्म फ़िल्टर के साथ ढूंढना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	bm_id8772545				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>searching; form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>removing;form filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering; data in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data;filtering in forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms; filtering data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data, see also values\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156042				0	hi	\<variable id=\"data_search2\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_search2.xhp\" name=\"Searching With a Form Filter\"\>Searching With a Form Filter\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	hi	फ़ॉर्म दस्तावेज़ खोलें जिसमें डाटाबेस क्षेत्र होते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	hi	As an example, open an empty text document and press F4. Open the bibliography database table \<emph\>biblio\</emph\> in the data source view. While pressing Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, drag a few column headers into the document so that the form fields are created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984	19			0	hi	On the \<emph\>Form Controls\</emph\> toolbar, click the \<emph\>Design Mode On/Off\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3147618\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_switchcontroldesignmode.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147618\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to turn off the design mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3148672	6			0	hi	On the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> toolbar, click the \<emph\>Form-Based Filters\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149807\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formfilter.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149807\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The current document is displayed with its form controls as an empty edit mask. The \<emph\>Form Filter \</emph\>toolbar appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666				0	hi	Enter the filter conditions into one or several fields. Note that if you enter filter conditions into several fields, all of the entered conditions must match (Boolean AND).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481	8			0	hi	More information about wildcards and operators can be found in \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Design\"\>Query Design\</link\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3152462				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilterExecute\"\>If you click the \<emph\>Apply Form-Based Filter\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Form Filter\</emph\> toolbar, the filter will be applied.\</ahelp\> You see the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> toolbar and can browse through the found records.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilterExit\"\>If you click on the \<emph\>Close\</emph\> button on the \<emph\>Form Filter\</emph\> toolbar, the form is displayed without a filter.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150114	11			0	hi	Click the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12120000.xhp\" name=\"Apply Filter\"\>\<emph\>Apply Filter\</emph\>\</link\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3144764\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_datafilterstandardfilter.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3144764\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> toolbar to change to the filtered view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search2.xhp	0	help	par_id3146898	12			0	hi	The filter that has been set can be removed by clicking \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12040000.xhp\" name=\"Remove Filter/Sort\"\>\<emph\>Remove Filter/Sort\</emph\>\</link\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3151318\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_removefiltersort.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151318\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
