helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	hi	खींचकर छोड़ने के जरिए नक़ल करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	hi	If you want to reverse a drag-and-drop, position the cursor in your document and choose \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	hi	It is also possible to copy by drag-and-drop from a document into a data source:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	hi	A text table or the selected range of a spreadsheet can be dragged using drag-and-drop to a table container in the data source explorer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211				0	hi	Plain text can be copied using drag-and-drop from one document to a data field in the data source view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145421				0	hi	पाठ दस्तावेज़ में डाटा इस्तेमाल करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685				0	hi	You can insert a database field in a text document by dragging a field name from the column header of the data source view into the document. This is especially useful when designing form letters. Simply drag the desired fields - home address, form of address, and so on - into your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153105				0	hi	To insert a complete record, select the corresponding header and drag it into the document. When you release the mouse button, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070000.xhp\" name=\"Insert database columns\"\>\<emph\>Insert database columns\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears, in which you can decide whether to use all database fields, and whether to copy the data into the document as text, a table or fields. All currently selected records will be inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147230				0	hi	तालिका दस्तावेज़ में डाटा लागू करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864				0	hi	You can insert one or more records into the current sheet of a spreadsheet by selecting the rows in the data source view and dragging and dropping them into the spreadsheet. The data is inserted at the place where you release the mouse button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149766				0	hi	पाठ फ़ॉर्म में नियंत्रण प्रविष्ट करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155132				0	hi	जब आप पाठ को किसी डाटा बेस कड़ी से बनाते हैं, आप डाटा स्रोत दृश्य से खींचकर-छोड़कर कंट्रोल बना सकते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149562				0	hi	When you drag a database column into the text document, you insert a field. If you hold down Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while dragging, a text field is inserted, grouped with an appropriate label field. The text field already contains all the database information that you need for the form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	पता किताब पंजीकृत करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152823				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>data sources; registering address books\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>address books; registering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>system address book registration\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>registering; address books\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154228				0	hi	\<variable id=\"data_addressbook\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_addressbook.xhp\" name=\"Registering an Address Book\"\>Registering an Address Book\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3154927				0	hi	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> you can register different data sources. The contents of the data fields are then available to you for use in various fields and controls. Your system address book is such a data source.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	hi	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> templates and wizards use fields for the contents of the address book. When activated, the general fields in the templates are automatically replaced with the fields from the data source of your address book.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	hi	In order for the replacement to take place, you must tell \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> which address book you use. The wizard asking for this information appears automatically the first time you activate, for example, a business letter template. You can also call the wizard by following the steps listed below.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id5941648				0	hi	The address book data is read-only in %PRODUCTNAME Base. It is not possible to add, edit, or delete address data from within Base.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149096				0	hi	Address Data Source Wizard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	hi	To call the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01170000.xhp\" name=\"Address Data Source\"\>Address Data Source\</link\> wizard, choose \<emph\>File - Wizards - Address Data Source\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	hi	मौजूदा पता पुस्तिका हस्तचालित पंजीकृत करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Address Book Source\</emph\>. The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110101.xhp\" name=\"Templates: Address Book Assignment\"\>\<emph\>Templates: Address Book Assignment\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	hi	In the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> combo box, select the system address book or the data source you want to use as an address book.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669	11			0	hi	If you have not yet registered the system address book in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> as the data source, click the \<emph\>Address Data Source ...\</emph\> button. This takes you to the \<emph\>Address Book Data Source Wizard\</emph\>, in which you can register your address book as a new data source in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	hi	In the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> combo box, select the database table you want to use as the address book.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084				0	hi	Under \<emph\>Field assignment\</emph\>, match the fields for first name, company, department, and so on to the actual field names used in your address book.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_idN10784				0	hi	When finished, close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149983				0	hi	Now your data source is registered in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> as the address book. If you now open a template from the \<emph\>Business Correspondence\</emph\> category, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> can automatically insert the correct fields for a form letter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	रेकॉर्ड सुरक्षित करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159201				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>changes; protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>protecting; recorded changes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>records; protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function;protecting records\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159201	1			0	hi	\<variable id=\"redlining_protect\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_protect.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Records\"\>Protecting Records\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id1631824				0	hi	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	hi	To protect the changes made in a document during editing, choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. To turn off the function or to accept or reject changes it is necessary to enter the correct password first.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Protect Records\</emph\>. This opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/password_dlg.xhp\" name=\"Password\"\>\<emph\>Password\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	hi	Enter a password consisting of at least 5 characters and confirm it. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
