helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AF				0	hi	Click the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> icon on the Standard toolbar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	hi	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+O 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	hi	The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>Open\</link\> dialog appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	hi	Select the file you want to open and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149234				0	hi	फ़ाइल को प्रदर्शन के लिए सीमित करें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985				0	hi	To restrict the display of files in the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> dialog to a certain type select the corresponding \<emph\>File type\</emph\> from the list. Select \<emph\>All Files (*.*)\</emph\> to display all files.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id4651326				0	hi	Cursor Position				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id5509201				0	hi	In general, all documents open with the cursor at the start of the document. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id6594744				0	hi	One exception appears when the author of a Writer text document saves and reopens a document: The cursor will be at the same position where it has been when the document was saved. This only works when the name of the author was entered in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - User Data\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3422650				0	hi	Press Shift+F5 to set the cursor to the last saved position.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148453				0	hi	रिक्त दस्तावेज़ खोलना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287				0	hi	Click the \<emph\>New\</emph\> icon on the Standard bar or choose \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>. This opens a document of the document type specified.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092				0	hi	If you click the arrow next to the \<emph\>New\</emph\> icon, a submenu opens in which you can select another document type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id0820200803501358				0	hi	System File Dialogs or %PRODUCTNAME Dialogs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501356				0	hi	On most operating systems, you can choose to use the system file dialogs or %PRODUCTNAME dialogs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501429				0	hi	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</item\> to switch the type of open/save dialogs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501449				0	hi	The %PRODUCTNAME dialogs support file download and upload using secure https connections.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id0820200803501453				0	hi	Opening Files from a Web Server				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126	9			0	hi	You can enter a URL in the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> dialogs. The URL must start with file:/// or ftp:// or http://. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200803501548				0	hi	If you use the %PRODUCTNAME dialog, you can use the https:// prefix for a secure connection, and you can save a document on the web server.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C4				0	hi	When you open a file by a URL from the Windows file dialog, Windows will open a local copy of the file, located in the Internet Explorer cache. The %PRODUCTNAME file dialog opens a local copy of the file in the system's temp folder.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3148616				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"File - Open\"\>File - Open\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	फ़ॉर्म दस्तावेज़ तथा तालिका ढूंढना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	bm_id4066896				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>finding;records in form documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms;finding records\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>searching;tables and forms\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154186				0	hi	\<variable id=\"data_search\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_search.xhp\" name=\"Searching Tables and Form Documents\"\>Searching Tables and Form Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	hi	\<image id=\"img_id3153311\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_recsearch.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153311\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3149178	65			0	hi	In spreadsheets and documents in which form controls are used, you can click the \<emph\>Find Record\</emph\> icon on the form bar to open a dialog to find any text and values. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_search.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	hi	You can search in one or in all data fields. You can select whether the text must be at the beginning, end or any location of the data field. You also can use the ? and * wildcards, as in the \<emph\>Find & Replace\</emph\> dialog. You can find additional information about the database search function in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12100200.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Help\"\>$[officename] Help\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	पाठ फ़ॉर्मेट में डाटा आयात तथा निर्यात करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	bm_id6911546				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>databases;importing/exporting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing;databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; datasource records in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; datasource records in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;inserting database records\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data sources;copying records to spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;from data sources to %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id4547257				0	hi	\<variable id=\"data_im_export\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_im_export.xhp\"\>Importing and Exporting Data in Base\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id2761314				0	hi	An easy method to import and export database tables uses Calc as a "helper application".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id3912778				0	hi	Exporting data from Base				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	hi	You copy a table from Base to a new Calc sheet, then you can save or export the data to any file format that Calc supports.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id121158				0	hi	Open the database file that contains the database table to be exported. Click Tables to view the tables, or click Queries to view the queries.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id4644306				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Spreadsheet\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id1331217				0	hi	In the Base window, right-click the name of the table to export. Choose \<emph\>Copy\</emph\> from the context menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3806878				0	hi	Click cell A1 in the new Calc window, then choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id130619				0	hi	Now you can save or export the data to many file types.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id9999694				0	hi	Importing data to Base				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id8494521				0	hi	You can import text files, spreadsheet files, and your system address book in read-only mode only. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id9579760				0	hi	When you import from a text or spreadsheet file, the file must have a first row of header information. The second row of the file is the first valid data row. The format of every field in the second row determines the format for the entire column. Any format information from a spreadsheet file gets lost when importing to Base.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id325632				0	hi	For example, to ensure the first column has a text format, you must make sure that the first field of the first valid data row contains text. If a field in the first valid data row contains a number, the whole column is set to number format, and only numbers, no text, will be shown in that column. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id2216559				0	hi	Open a Base file of the database type that you want. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id7869502				0	hi	Either create a new Base file using the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabawiz00.xhp\"\>Database Wizard\</link\>, or open any existing Base file that is not read-only.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id9852900				0	hi	Open the Calc file that contains the data to be imported to Base. You can open a *.dbf dBASE file or many other file types. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3791924				0	hi	Select the data to be copied to Base. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id6173894				0	hi	You can enter a range reference like A1:X500 in the Name Box if you don't want to scroll.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id533768				0	hi	If you copy a dBASE sheet, include the top row that contains the header data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id5669423				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Copy\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id3619495				0	hi	In the Base window, click \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> to view the tables.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id1175572				0	hi	In the Base window, choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id4815820				0	hi	You see the Copy Table dialog. Most databases need a primary key, so you may want to check the \<emph\>Create primary key\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_im_export.xhp	0	help	par_id2584002				0	hi	On Windows systems, you can also use drag-and-drop instead of Copy and Paste. Also, for registered databases, you can open the datasource browser (press F4) instead of opening the Base window.				20200411 15:09:53
