helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\macrosecurity.xhp	0	help	par_idN1056A				0	hi	The Macro Security dialog appears when a document contains one or more macros. You can also call the dialog from the \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01030300.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Security\</link\>\</emph\> page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01090000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	सूत्र				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150040				0	hi	%PRODUCTNAME Math Options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	hi	\<variable id=\"druckentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SmEditOptions\"\>Defines the print format and print options for all new formula documents. These options apply when you print a formula directly from \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Math.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> You can also call the dialog by clicking the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> button in the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog. The settings you define in the \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\</emph\> dialog will be permanent settings, whereas the settings in the Print dialog are only valid for the current document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154143				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01090100.xhp\" name=\"Options\"\>Options\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
