helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707	28			0	hi	         \<emph\>Example:\</emph\> Type the text 'Test' in cell A1; and the text 'test' in B1. Then type the formula "=A1=B1" in cell C1. If the \<emph\>Case sensitive\</emph\> box is marked, FALSE will appear in the cell; otherwise, TRUE will appear in the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01060500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965				0	hi	The EXACT text function is always case-sensitive, independent of the settings in this dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
