helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3157898				0	hi	When you create a database table as an administrator, you can use this tab to determine user access, and to edit the data or the table structure.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05040100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152594				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>access rights for database tables (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables in databases; access rights to (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152594				0	hi	If you are not the administrator, you can use the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab to view your access rights for the selected table.				20200411 15:09:53
