helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05040100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153126				0	hi	संदर्भ परिवर्धित करें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3159399				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Allows the user to modify the defined references, for example, to enter new relations for the table or to delete existing relations.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	Report Builder				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	bm_id1614429				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>Report Builder\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Apache OpenOffice Report Builder\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	hd_id8773155				0	hi	\<variable id=\"rep_main\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Builder\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id5248573				0	hi	The Report Builder is a tool to create your own database reports. Unlike with the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01100000.xhp\"\>Report Wizard\</link\>, using the Report Builder you can take control to design the report the way you want. The generated report is a Writer document that you can edit, too.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7128818				0	hi	To use the Report Builder, the Report Builder extension must be installed. In addition, the Java Runtime Environment (JRE) software must be installed, and this software must be selected in %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	hd_id3753776				0	hi	To Install the Report Builder Extension				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id5284279				0	hi	Choose Tools - Extension Manager to open the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/packagemanager.xhp\"\>Extension Manager\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id4494766				0	hi	If you see the Report Builder in the Extension Manager list, then you do not need to install the extension. Else click the link "Get more extensions here". This opens your web browser at the address \<link href=\"http://extensions.openoffice.org\"\>http://extensions.openoffice.org\</link\> and shows a list of available extensions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7858516				0	hi	Find the Report Builder extension. Click at the icon or the "click here" text link. This opens the download page for the extension.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id973540				0	hi	Click the "Get it!" icon. The extension file will be downloaded to your computer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id4680928				0	hi	Switch back from your web browser to the %PRODUCTNAME window. The Extension Manager should still be visible.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id9014252				0	hi	In the Extension Manager, click Add to open the Add extensions dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id6011841				0	hi	Select the extension file that you downloaded. Click Open.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id2591326				0	hi	This starts the installation of the Report Builder extension.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id6201666				0	hi	Read the license. If you accept the license, click Accept to continue the installation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id208136				0	hi	Click Close to close the Extension Manager.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id20813699				0	hi	Restart %PRODUCTNAME. If the Quickstarter is running, also close the Quickstarter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	hd_id556047				0	hi	To install the JRE software				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id4515823				0	hi	The Report Builder requires an installed Java Runtime Environment (JRE).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id4044312				0	hi	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/java.xhp\"\>Java\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id1369060				0	hi	Wait up to one minute, while %PRODUCTNAME collects information on installed Java software on your system.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id860927				0	hi	If a recent JRE version is found on your system, you see an entry in the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id8581804				0	hi	Click the option button in front of the entry to enable this JRE version for use in %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7730033				0	hi	Ensure that \<emph\>Use a Java runtime environment\</emph\> is enabled.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id6317636				0	hi	If no JRE version is found on your system, open your web browser and download the JRE software from \<link href=\"http://www.java.com\"\>http://www.java.com\</link\>. Install the JRE software. Then restart %PRODUCTNAME and open \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Java again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	hd_id9759514				0	hi	To open the Report Builder				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id9076509				0	hi	Open a Base file or create a new database. The database must contain at least one table with at least one data field and a primary key field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7050691				0	hi	Click the Reports icon in the Base window, then choose Create Report in Design View.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7118747				0	hi	The Report Builder window opens. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id8283639				0	hi	The Report Builder is divided into three parts. On the top you see the menu, with the toolbars below.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id2291024				0	hi	On the right you see the Properties window with the property values of the currently selected object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id2100589				0	hi	The left part of the Report Builder window shows the Report Builder view. The Report Builder view is initially divided into three sections, from top to bottom:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id5022125				0	hi	               \<emph\>Page Header\</emph\> - drag control fields with fixed text into the Page Header area				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id6844386				0	hi	               \<emph\>Detail\</emph\> - drag and drop database fields into the Detail area				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7018646				0	hi	               \<emph\>Page Footer\</emph\> - drag control fields with fixed text into the Page Footer area				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id5857112				0	hi	To insert an additional \<emph\>Report Header\</emph\> and \<emph\>Report Footer\</emph\> area choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Insert Report Header/Footer\</item\>. These areas contain text that appears at the start and end of the whole report.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id6042664				0	hi	Click the "-" icon in front of an area name to collapse that area to one line in the Report Builder view. The "-" icon changes to a "+" icon, and you can click this to expand the area again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id1589098				0	hi	You insert database fields by drag-and-drop into the Detail area. See the section "To insert fields into the report" below.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id1278420				0	hi	In addition, you can click the Label Field or Text Box icon in the toolbar, then drag a rectangle in the Page Header or Page Footer area, to define a text that is the same on all pages. You enter the text in the Label box of the corresponding Properties window. You can also add graphics by using the Graphics icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7479476				0	hi	To connect the report to a database table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id3099154				0	hi	First you must connect the report to a database table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id2218390				0	hi	Move the mouse to the Properties view. You see two tab pages General and Data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7771538				0	hi	On the Data tab page, click Content to open the combo box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id366527				0	hi	Select the table for that you want to create the report.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7996459				0	hi	After selecting the table, press the Tab key to leave the Content box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id2531815				0	hi	The Add Field window opens automatically and shows all fields of the selected table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id5927304				0	hi	To insert fields into the report				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id4503921				0	hi	The Add Field window helps you to insert the table entries in the report. Click the Add Field icon in the toolbar to open the Add Field window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id4051026				0	hi	Drag and drop the field names one by one from the Add Field window into the Detail area of the report. Position the fields as you like. Use the icons in the toolbars to align the fields.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id3397320				0	hi	It is not possible to overlap the fields. If you drop a table field on the Detail area, then a label and a text box are inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id3059785				0	hi	You can also insert text that should be the same on every page of the report. Click the Label Field icon\<image id=\"img_id5605334\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_label.png\" width=\"0.566cm\" height=\"0.566cm\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5605334\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>, then drag a rectangle in the Page Header or Page Footer area. Edit the Label property to show the text you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7657399				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select two or more objects and click this icon to align the objects at the left margin of the area.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id8925138				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select two or more objects and click this icon to align the objects at the right margin of the area.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id5461897				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select two or more objects and click this icon to align the objects at the top margin of the area.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id8919339				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select two or more objects and click this icon to align the objects at the bottom margin of the area.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id4634235				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select two or more objects and click this icon to resize the objects to the smallest width.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id1393475				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select two or more objects and click this icon to resize the objects to the smallest height.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id6571550				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select two or more objects and click this icon to resize the objects to the greatest width.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id5376140				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select two or more objects and click this icon to resize the objects to the greatest height.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id9611499				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts a horizontal line to the current area.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id6765953				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts a vertical line to the current area.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200922242612				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shrinks the selected section to remove top and bottom empty space.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200922242617				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shrinks the selected section to remove top empty space.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200922242661				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shrinks the selected section to remove bottom empty space.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id1511581				0	hi	After inserting fields in the Detail view, the report is ready for execution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id4881740				0	hi	To execute a report				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id8286385				0	hi	Click the Execute Report icon\<image id=\"img_id3380230\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_executereport.png\" width=\"0.566cm\" height=\"0.566cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3380230\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id2354197				0	hi	A Writer document opens and shows the report you have created, which contains all values of the database table which you have insert.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id2485122				0	hi	If the database contents did change, execute the report again to update the result report.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	hd_id8746910				0	hi	To edit a report				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id9636524				0	hi	First decide if you want to edit the generated report, which is a static Writer document, or if you want to edit the Report Builder view and then generate a new report based on the new design.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id5941648				0	hi	The Writer document is opened read-only. To edit the Writer document, click Edit File\<image id=\"img_id8237556\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_editdoc.png\" width=\"0.566cm\" height=\"0.566cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id8237556\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the Standard toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id8307138				0	hi	If you want to edit the Report Builder view, you can change some of its properties.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7138889				0	hi	Click in the Details area. Then in the Properties window, change some properties, for example the background color.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id9869380				0	hi	After finishing, click the Execute Report icon\<image id=\"Graphic2\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_executereport.png\" width=\"0.566cm\" height=\"0.566cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to create a new report.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id12512				0	hi	If you close the Report Builder, you will be asked if the report should be saved. Click Yes, give the report a name, and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id2676168				0	hi	Sorting the report				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id2626422				0	hi	Without sorting or grouping, the records will be inserted into the report in the order in which they are retrieved from the database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id1743827				0	hi	Open the Report Builder view and click the Sorting and Grouping icon\<image id=\"img_id9557786\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_dbsortingandgrouping.png\" width=\"0.566cm\" height=\"0.566cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id9557786\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the toolbar. You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_sort.xhp\"\>Sorting and Grouping\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id4331797				0	hi	In the Groups box, click the field which you want as the first sort field, and set the Sorting property.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id4191717				0	hi	Execute the report.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id2318796				0	hi	Grouping				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id399182				0	hi	Open the Report Builder view and click the Sorting and Grouping icon\<image id=\"Graphic21\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_dbsortingandgrouping.png\" width=\"0.566cm\" height=\"0.566cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the toolbar. You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_sort.xhp\"\>Sorting and Grouping\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7588732				0	hi	In the Groups box, open the Group Header list box and select to show a group header.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id95828				0	hi	Click the Add Field icon\<image id=\"Graphic3\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_addfield.png\" width=\"0.566cm\" height=\"0.566cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to open the Add Field window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id5675527				0	hi	Drag-and-drop the field entry that you want to group into the group header section. Then drag-and-drop the remaining fields into the Detail section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id3496200				0	hi	Execute the report. The report shows the grouped records.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7599108				0	hi	If you like to sort and group, open the Report Builder view, then open the Sorting and Grouping dialog. Select to show a Group Header for the fields that you want to group, and select to hide the Group Header for the fields that you want to be sorted. Close the Sorting and Grouping window and execute the report.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id888698				0	hi	Updating and printing your data				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id3394573				0	hi	When you insert some new data or edit data in the table, a new report will show the updated data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7594225				0	hi	Click the Reports icon\<image id=\"img_id4678487\" src=\"dbaccess/res/reports_32.png\" width=\"0.566cm\" height=\"0.566cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4678487\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and double-click your last saved report. A new Writer document will be created which shows the new data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id8147221				0	hi	To print a report, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Print\</item\> from the Writer document.				20200411 15:09:53
