helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	par_id3150249				0	hi	इसे करने के लिए, आपको रिक्त समूह तथा अक्षर वाक्यांश निर्धारित करना होगा. इन्हें किसी जगह की आवश्यकता नहीं होती है, परंतु ये वे जानकारियाँ रखते हैं जो पंक्तिबद्धता प्रक्रिया में मदद करते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	par_id3153912				0	hi	To create empty groups, enter curly brackets \<emph\>{}\</emph\> in the Commands window. In the following example, the goal is to achieve a line break so that the plus signs are beneath one another, even though one less character is entered in the upper line:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	par_id3153246				0	hi	a+a+a+{} newline {}{}{}{}{}a+a+a+a				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	par_id3143229				0	hi	Empty character strings are a simple way to ensure that texts and formulas are left-aligned. They are defined using double inverted commas "" . Make sure you do not use any typographic inverted commas. Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\align.xhp	0	help	par_id3153809				0	hi	"एक अन्य उदाहरण." newline a+b newline ""c-d				20200411 15:09:53
