helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id5154576				0	hi	Standard Error: Displays the standard error.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3157979				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Variance: Displays the variance calculated from the number of data points and respective values.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153249				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Standard Deviation: Displays the standard deviation (square root of the variance).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149870				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Error Margin: Displays the highest error margin in percent according to the highest value of the data group. Set the percentage in the Parameters area.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id350962				0	hi	Cell Range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id6679586				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click Cell Range and then specify a cell range from which to take the positive and negative error bar values.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3872188				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click a button to shrink the dialog, then use the mouse to select the cell range in the spreadsheet. Click the button again to restore the dialog to full size.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id2633747				0	hi	From Data Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id6633503				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For a chart with its own data, the error bar values can be entered in the chart data table. The Data Table dialog shows additional columns titled Positive Y-Error-Bars and Negative Y-Error-Bars.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573839				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the value to add to the displayed value as the positive error value.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573862				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the value to subtract from the displayed value as the negative error value.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573844				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the address range from where to get the positive error values. Use the Shrink button to select the range from a sheet.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573970				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the address range from where to get the negative error values. Use the Shrink button to select the range from a sheet.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0428200810573977				0	hi	Same value for both				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573991				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enable to use the positive error values also as negative error values. You can only change the value of the "Positve (+)" box. That value gets copied to the "Negative (-)" box automatically.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
