helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145253				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>presentations;rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>timings; rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic slide changes;rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recording;display times for slides\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145253				0	hi	\<variable id=\"rehearse_timings\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/rehearse_timings.xhp\" name=\"Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes\"\>Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446	1			0	hi	$[officename] assists you in defining the right rehearse timings for automatic slide changes. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	hi	Prepare the slides, start the show using a special icon, tell your imaginary audience what you want to tell for the first slide, then advance to the next slide and so on. $[officename] records the display time for each slide, so the next time you play the show with automatic slide changes, the timing will be as recorded.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146317				0	hi	To record a show with rehearse timings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874				0	hi	Open a presentation, and switch to \<emph\>Slide Sorter\</emph\> View.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150651	6			0	hi	Start the show with the \<emph\>Rehearse Timings\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156396\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_rehearsetimings.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156396\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the Slide View bar. You see the first slide, and a timer in the bottom corner.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3145590				0	hi	When it's time to advance to the next slide, click the timer. To keep the default setting for this slide, click the slide, but not the timer. Continue for all slides in your presentation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150333				0	hi	$[officename] has recorded the display time for each slide. Save your presentation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3145248				0	hi	If you want the whole presentation to auto-repeat, open the menu \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show Settings\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Auto\</emph\> and \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150935				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Slide Show Settings\"\>Slide Show Settings\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
