helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150021				0	hi	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145244				0	hi	स्लाइड पृष्ठभूमि के लिए छवि इस्तेमाल करने के लिए				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3148394				0	hi	You can display an entire image as a slide background, or you can tile the image to produce a patterned background.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3156064				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click on the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3145356	59			0	hi	In the \<emph\>Fill \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>Bitmap\</emph\>, and then click an image in the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150757	60			0	hi	If you want to use a custom image for the slide background, close the \<emph\>Page Setup \</emph\>dialog, and then choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>. Click the \<emph\>Bitmaps \</emph\>tab, and then click \<emph\>Import\</emph\>. Locate the image you want to import and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. When you return to the \<emph\>Background \</emph\>tab, the image you imported will be in the \<emph\>Bitmap \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3153151				0	hi	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150263	62			0	hi	To display the entire image as the background, clear the \<emph\>Tile \</emph\>check box in the \<emph\>Position \</emph\>area, and then select \<emph\>AutoFit\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149756				0	hi	To tile the image on the background, select \<emph\>Tile\</emph\>, and set the \<emph\>Size\</emph\>, \<emph\>Position\</emph\>, and \<emph\>Offset\</emph\> options for the image.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3154934				0	hi	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3158403				0	hi	परिवर्धन सिर्फ वर्तमान प्रेज़ेन्टेशन दस्तावेज़ के लिए वैध हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10820				0	hi	To save a new slide master as a template				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10827				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\> to change to the slide master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\> to change the slide background, or choose other formatting commands. Objects that you add here will be visible on all slides that are based on this slide master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\> to close the master view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN1083F				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\> to save the document as a template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10847				0	hi	Enter a name for the template. Do not change the category from "My Templates". Click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084A				0	hi	Now you can use the Presentation Wizard to open a new presentation based on your new template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	Using Gluepoints				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	bm_id0919200803534995				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>glue points;using\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	hi	\<variable id=\"gluepoints\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/gluepoints.xhp\"\>Using Gluepoints\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803040964				0	hi	In Impress and Draw, you can connect each two shapes with a line called a \<link href=\"text/simpress/02/10100000.xhp\"\>connector\</link\>. When you draw a connector between shapes, the connector will be attached to a gluepoint on each shape. Each shape has some default gluepoints, and the positions of the default gluepoints depend on the specific shape. You can add your own custom gluepoints to a shape and then attach connectors to the custom gluepoints.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041099				0	hi	To add and edit gluepoints				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id091920080304108				0	hi	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041082				0	hi	Click the \<emph\>Glue Point\</emph\> icon on the Drawing toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041186				0	hi	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Glue Points\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041160				0	hi	Click the \<emph\>Insert Glue Point\</emph\> icon on the Gluepoints toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041115				0	hi	Click inside the shape where you want to add the new gluepoint.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041133				0	hi	If the shape is filled, you can click anywhere inside the shape. If the shape is unfilled, you can click the border to insert a glue point. Once inserted, you can drag the glue point to another position inside the shape.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041250				0	hi	With the four icons next to the \<emph\>Insert Glue Point\</emph\> icon, you choose the directions which will be permitted for a connector at this gluepoint. You can choose one or more directions for a particular gluepoint.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041298				0	hi	If the \<emph\>Glue Point Relative\</emph\> icon is active, the gluepoint moves when you resize the object to keep its position relative to the object borders.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041223				0	hi	If the \<emph\>Glue Point Relative\</emph\> icon is not active, the icons next to it are no longer grayed out. With these icons you can decide where a gluepoint will be placed when the size of the object is changed.				20200411 15:09:53
