helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3153969				0	hi	आप $[officename] कॅल्क में उपयोक्ता-निर्धारित फ़ंक्शन निम्न तरीके से लागू कर सकते हैं:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	hi	You can define your own functions using the Basic-IDE. This method requires a basic knowledge of programming.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	hi	You can program functions as \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060111.xhp\" name=\"add-ins\"\>add-ins\</link\>. This method requires an advanced knowledge of programming.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149260				0	hi	Defining A Function Using %PRODUCTNAME Basic				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456				0	hi	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	hi	Click the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> button. You will now see the Basic IDE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327				0	hi	Enter the function code. In this example, we define a \<item type=\"literal\"\>VOL(a; b; c)\</item\> function that calculates the volume of a rectangular solid with side lengths \<item type=\"literal\"\>a\</item\>, \<item type=\"literal\"\>b\</item\> and \<item type=\"literal\"\>c\</item\>:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	hi	बेसिक-आईडीई विंडो चुनें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150043				0	hi	Your function is automatically saved in the default module and is now available. If you apply the function in a Calc document that is to be used on another computer, you can copy the function to the Calc document as described in the next section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147340				0	hi	फ़ंक्शन को किसी दस्तावेज़ में नक़ल करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3145232	19			0	hi	In stage 2 of "Defining A Function Using %PRODUCTNAME Basic", in the \<emph\>Macro\</emph\> dialog you clicked on \<emph\>Edit \</emph\>. As the default, in the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> field the \<emph\>My Macros - Standard - Module1\</emph\> module is selected. The \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> library resides locally in your user directory.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	hi	यदि आप उपयोक्ता पारिभाषित फंक्शन को किसी कॅल्क दस्तावेज़ में नक़ल करना चाहते हैं:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	hi	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</item\> .				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150086				0	hi	In the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> field select \<emph\>My Macros - Standard - Module1\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3166430				0	hi	In the Basic-IDE, select the source of your user-defined function and copy it to the clipboard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081D				0	hi	बेसिक आईडीई बन्द करें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150517				0	hi	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</item\> .				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	hi	In the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> field select \<emph\>(Name of the Calc document) - Standard - Module1\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148699				0	hi	बेसिक आईडीई दस्तावेज़ में क्लिपबोर्ड सामग्री को चिपकाएँ				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153305				0	hi	$[officename] कॅल्क में उपयोक्ता पारिभाषित फ़ंक्शन लागू करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148869				0	hi	Once you have defined the function \<item type=\"literal\"\>VOL(a; b; c)\</item\> in the Basic-IDE, you can apply it the same way as the built-in functions of $[officename] Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148606				0	hi	Open a Calc document and enter numbers for the function parameters \<item type=\"literal\"\>a\</item\>, \<item type=\"literal\"\>b\</item\>, and \<item type=\"literal\"\>c\</item\> in cells A1, B1, and C1.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3156019				0	hi	संकेतक को किसी अन्य कक्ष में सेट करें व निम्न प्रविष्ट करें:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3155264				0	hi	=VOL(A1;B1;C1)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3146776				0	hi	फ़ंक्शन का मूल्यांकन किया गया तथा परिणाम आप चयनित कक्ष में देख सकते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	पाठ फ़ाइलें आयात तथा निर्यात करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153726				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>csv files;formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas; importing/exporting as csv files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>exporting;formulas as csv files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>importing;csv files with formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726				0	hi	\<variable id=\"csv_formula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/csv_formula.xhp\" name=\"Importing and Exporting Text Files\"\>Importing and Exporting CSV Text Files with Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149402				0	hi	Comma separated values (CSV) files are text files that contain the cell contents of a single sheet. Commas, semicolons, or other characters can be used as the field delimiters between the cells. Text strings are put in quotation marks, numbers are written without quotation marks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715				0	hi	To Import a CSV File				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153709				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155445				0	hi	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> field, select the format "Text CSV". Select the file and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. When a file has the .csv extension, the file type is automatically recognized.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	hi	You will see the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Import\</item\> dialog. Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149255				0	hi	If the csv file contains formulas, but you want to import the results of those formulas, then choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154022				0	hi	To Export Formulas and Values as CSV Files				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	hi	शीट को क्लिक करें csv के रूप में लिखने के लिए.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3166423				0	hi	यदि आप सूत्रों को सूत्रों के रूप में निर्यात करना चाहते हैं, उदाहरण के लिए, इस फ़ॉर्म में =SUM(A1:B5), तो निम्न रूप में आगे बढ़ें:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155111				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150200				0	hi	Under \<emph\>Display\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	hi	If you want to export the calculation results instead of the formulas, do not mark \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3148702				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Save as\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153912				0	hi	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File type\</item\> field select the format "Text CSV".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3157978				0	hi	Enter a name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	hi	From the \<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\> dialog that appears, select the character set and the field and text delimiters for the data to be exported, and confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3146781				0	hi	If the numbers use commas as decimal separators or thousands separators, do not select the comma as the field delimiter. If the text contains double quotation marks, you must select the single quotation mark as separator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150050				0	hi	If necessary, after you have saved, clear the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box to see the calculated results in the table again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153487				0	hi	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153008				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000207.xhp\" name=\"Export text files\"\>Export text files\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
