helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10738				0	hi	\<variable id=\"dbase_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/dbase_files.xhp\"\>Importing and Exporting dBASE Files\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10756				0	hi	You can open and save data in the dBASE file format (*.dbf file extension) in $[officename] Base or a spreadsheet. In %PRODUCTNAME Base, a dBASE database is a folder that contains files with the .dbf file extension. Each file corresponds to a table in the database. Formulas and formatting are lost when you open and save a dBASE file from %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10759				0	hi	To Import a dBASE File Into a Spreadsheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071F				0	hi	*.dbf फ़ाइल को ढूंढें जिसे आप आयात करना चाहते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10768				0	hi	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10730				0	hi	The \<emph\>Import dBASE files\</emph\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	hi	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10777				0	hi	The dBASE file opens as a new Calc spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074E				0	hi	If you want to save the spreadsheet as a dBASE file, do not alter or delete the first row in the imported file. This row contains information that is required by a dBASE database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077A				0	hi	To Import a dBASE File Into a Database Table				20200411 15:09:53
