helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153361				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>cells; selecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>marking cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>selecting;cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>multiple cells selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>selection modes in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; selecting ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153361				0	hi	\<variable id=\"mark_cells\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/mark_cells.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Multiple Cells\"\>Selecting Multiple Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145272				0	hi	आयताकार दायरा चुनें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149261				0	hi	With the mouse button pressed, drag from one corner to the diagonally opposed corner of the range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151119				0	hi	एकल कक्ष को चिह्नित करें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	hi	निम्न में से कोई एक करें:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	hi	क्लिक करें, फिर कक्ष को शिफ़्ट-क्लिक करें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	hi	Pressing the mouse button, drag a range across two cells, do not release the mouse button, and then drag back to the first cell. Release the mouse button. You can now move the individual cell by drag and drop.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154942				0	hi	विविध डिस्पर्स्ड कक्षों को चुनें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id1001200901072060				0	hi	निम्न में से कोई एक करें:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284				0	hi	Mark at least one cell. Then while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, click each of the additional cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id1001200901072023				0	hi	Click the STD / EXT / ADD area in the status bar until it shows ADD. Now click all cells that you want to select.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146971				0	hi	मार्किंग मोड स्विच करें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	hi	On the status bar, click the box with the legend STD / EXT / ADD to switch the marking mode:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3159264				0	hi	क्षेत्र की सामग्रियाँ				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155337				0	hi	माउस क्लिक करने का प्रभाव				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568				0	hi	STD				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3148486				0	hi	किसी कक्ष में क्लिक करने पर उसे चुन लिया जाता है, तथा सभी चिह्नित कक्षों को अचिह्नित करता है.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090				0	hi	EXT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3150305				0	hi	A mouse click marks a rectangular range from the current cell to the cell you clicked. Alternatively, Shift-click a cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587				0	hi	ADD				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	hi	A mouse click in a cell adds it to the already marked cells. A mouse click in a marked cell unmarks it. Alternatively, \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>-click the cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3154487				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/scalc/main0208.xhp\" name=\"Status bar\"\>Status bar\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	छांटने की सूची लागू करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150870				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>filling;customized lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sort lists;applying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;sort lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>geometric lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arithmetic lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>series;sort lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists; user-defined\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>customized lists\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150870	3			0	hi	\<variable id=\"sorted_list\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/sorted_list.xhp\" name=\"Applying Sort Lists\"\>Applying Sort Lists\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3159154				0	hi	Sort lists allow you to type one piece of information in a cell, then drag it to fill in a consecutive list of items.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	hi	For example, enter the text "Jan" or "January" in an empty cell. Select the cell and click the mouse on the lower right corner of the cell border. Then drag the selected cell a few cells to the right or downwards. When you release the mouse button, the highlighted cells will be filled with the names of the months.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id2367931				0	hi	Hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>if you do not want to fill the cells with different values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577				0	hi	The predefined series can be found under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists\</emph\>. You can also create your own lists of text strings tailored to your needs, such as a list of your company's branch offices. When you use the information in these lists later (for example, as headings), just enter the first name in the list and expand the entry by dragging it with your mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060400.xhp\" name=\"Sort lists\"\>Sort lists\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	Converting Text to Numbers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>formats; text as numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>time format conversion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>date formats;conversion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>converting;text, into numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id0908200901265171				0	hi	\<variable id=\"numbers_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/numbers_text.xhp\" name=\"Converting Text to Numbers\"\>Converting Text to Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265127				0	hi	Calc converts text inside cells to the respective numeric values if an unambiguous conversion is possible. If no conversion is possible, Calc returns a #VALUE! error.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265196				0	hi	Only integer numbers including exponent are converted, and ISO 8601 dates and times in their extended formats with separators. Anything else, like fractional numbers with decimal separators or dates other than ISO 8601, is not converted, as the text string would be locale dependent. Leading and trailing blanks are ignored.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265220				0	hi	The following ISO 8601 formats are converted:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265288				0	hi	CCYY-MM-DD				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265267				0	hi	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265248				0	hi	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265374				0	hi	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss,s				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265327				0	hi	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss.s				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265399				0	hi	hh:mm				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265347				0	hi	hh:mm:ss				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265349				0	hi	hh:mm:ss,s				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265342				0	hi	hh:mm:ss.s				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265491				0	hi	The century code CC may not be omitted. Instead of the T date and time separator, exactly one space character may be used.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265467				0	hi	If a date is given, it must be a valid Gregorian calendar date. In this case the optional time must be in the range 00:00 to 23:59:59.99999...				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265420				0	hi	If only a time string is given, it may have an hours value of more than 24, while minutes and seconds can have a maximum value of 59.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265448				0	hi	The conversion is done for single arguments only, as in =A1+A2, or ="1E2"+1. Cell range arguments are not affected, so SUM(A1:A2) differs from A1+A2 if at least one of the two cells contain a convertible string.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id090820090126540				0	hi	Strings inside formulas are also converted, such as in ="1999-11-22"+42, which returns the date 42 days after November 22nd, 1999. Calculations involving localized dates as strings inside the formula return an error. For example, the localized date string "11/22/1999" or "22.11.1999" cannot be used for the automatic conversion.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id1005200903485368				0	hi	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id1005200903485359				0	hi	In A1 enter the text \<item type=\"literal\"\>'1e2\</item\> (which is converted to the number 100 internally).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id1005200903485341				0	hi	In A2 enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>=A1+1\</item\> (which correctly results in 101).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265544				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Numbers\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	ऋणात्मक संख्याएँ उभारना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147434				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; highlighting negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>highlighting;negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>colors;negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number formats;colors for negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434				0	hi	\<variable id=\"cellstyle_minusvalue\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp\" name=\"Highlighting Negative Numbers\"\>Highlighting Negative Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	hi	You can format cells with a number format that highlights negative numbers in red. Alternatively, you can define your own number format in which negative numbers are highlighted in other colors.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	hi	Select the cells and choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	hi	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab, select a number format and mark \<emph\>Negative numbers red\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	hi	The cell number format is defined in two parts. The format for positive numbers and zero is defined in front of the semicolon; after the semicolon the formula for negative numbers is defined. You can change the code (RED) under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format code\</item\>. For example, instead of RED, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>YELLOW\</item\>. If the new code appears in the list after clicking the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Add\</item\> icon, this is a valid entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	कक्ष को अन्य दस्तावेज़ में संदर्भित करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147436				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>sheet references\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references; to cells in other sheets/documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; operating in another document\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents;references\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436				0	hi	\<variable id=\"cellreferences\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences.xhp\" name=\"Referencing Other Sheets\"\>Referencing Other Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9663075				0	hi	किसी शीट कक्ष में आप अन्य शीट के कक्ष का संदर्भ दिखा सकते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id1879329				0	hi	In the same way, a reference can also be made to a cell from another document provided that this document has already been saved as a file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id7122409				0	hi	कक्ष को अन्य दस्तावेज़ में संदर्भित करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id2078005				0	hi	एक नया खाली स्प्रेडशीट खोलें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id4943693				0	hi	उदाहरण के द्वारा, निम्न सूत्र को शीट 1 के कक्ष A1 में भरें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9064302				0	hi	               \<item type=\"literal\"\>=Sheet2.A1\</item\>            				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7609790				0	hi	Click the \<emph\>Sheet 2\</emph\> tab at the bottom of the spreadsheet. Set the cursor in cell A1 there and enter text or a number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id809961				0	hi	If you switch back to Sheet1, you will see the same content in cell A1 there. If the contents of Sheet2.A1 change, then the contents of Sheet1.A1 also change.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id9209570				0	hi	कक्ष को अन्य दस्तावेज़ में संदर्भित करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5949278				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>, to load an existing spreadsheet document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8001953				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, to open a new spreadsheet document. Set the cursor in the cell where you want to insert the external data and enter an equals sign to indicate that you want to begin a formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8571123				0	hi	Now switch to the document you have just loaded. Click the cell with the data that you want to insert in the new document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8261665				0	hi	Switch back to the new spreadsheet. In the input line you will now see how $[officename] Calc has added the reference to the formula for you. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5888241				0	hi	The reference to a cell of another document contains the name of the other document in single inverted commas, then a hash #, then the name of the sheet of the other document, followed by a point and the name of the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7697683				0	hi	हरा चेक मार्क को क्लिक कर सूत्र की पुष्टि करें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7099826				0	hi	If you drag the box in the lower right corner of the active cell to select a range of cells, $[officename] automatically inserts the corresponding references in the adjacent cells. As a result, the sheet name is preceded with a "$" sign to designate it as an absolute reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id674459				0	hi	If you examine the name of the other document in this formula, you will notice that it is written as a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>URL\</link\>. This means that you can also enter a URL from the Internet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	बहुल ऑपरेशन लागू करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147559				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>multiple operations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>what if operations;two variables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-classified tables\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147559				0	hi	\<variable id=\"multioperation\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multioperation.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Operations\"\>Applying Multiple Operations\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145171				0	hi	पंक्तियों और स्तंभों के बीच बहुल ऑपरेशन				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id4123966				0	hi	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Multiple Operations\</item\> command provides a planning tool for "what if" questions. In your spreadsheet, you enter a formula to calculate a result from values that are stored in other cells. Then, you set up a cell range where you enter some fixed values, and the Multiple Operations command will calculate the results depending on the formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	hi	In the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field, enter the cell reference to the formula that applies to the data range. In the \<emph\>Column input cell/Row input cell\</emph\> field, enter the cell reference to the corresponding cell that is part of the formula. This can be explained best by examples:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159153				0	hi	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153189				0	hi	You produce toys which you sell for $10 each. Each toy costs $2 to make, in addition to which you have fixed costs of $10,000 per year. How much profit will you make in a year if you sell a particular number of toys?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id6478774				0	hi	\<image id=\"img_id1621753\" src=\"res/helpimg/what-if.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1621753\"\>what-if sheet area\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145239				0	hi	एक वेरिएबल तथा एक सूत्र से गणना करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146888				0	hi	To calculate the profit, first enter any number as the quantity (items sold) - in this example 2000. The profit is found from the formula Profit=Quantity * (Selling price - Direct costs) - Fixed costs. Enter this formula in B5.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3157875				0	hi	In column D enter given annual sales, one below the other; for example, 500 to 5000, in steps of 500.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3159115				0	hi	Select the range D2:E11, and thus the values in column D and the empty cells alongside in column E.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149723				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple operations\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149149	46			0	hi	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas \</emph\>field, click cell B5.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149355				0	hi	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> field and click cell B4. This means that B4, the quantity, is the variable in the formula, which is replaced by the selected column values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149009				0	hi	Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You see the profits for the different quantities in column E.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148725				0	hi	एक साथ ही बहुत सारे सूत्रों में गणना करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146880				0	hi	स्तम्भ E मिटाएँ.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154675				0	hi	 C5 में निम्न सूत्र प्रविष्ट करें: = B5 / B4. अब आप प्रति वस्तु विक्रय पर वार्षिक लाभ की गणना कर रहे हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3148885				0	hi	Select the range D2:F11, thus three columns.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3147474				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple Operations\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154846				0	hi	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field, select cells B5 through C5.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153931				0	hi	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> field and click cell B4.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3150862				0	hi	Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You will now see the profits in column E and the annual profit per item in column F.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146139				0	hi	पंक्तियों और स्तंभों के बीच बहुल ऑपरेशन				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3148584				0	hi	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> allows you to carry out joint multiple operations for columns and rows in so-called cross-tables. The formula cell has to refer to both the data range arranged in rows and the one arranged in columns. Select the range defined by both data ranges and call the multiple operation dialog. Enter the reference to the formula in the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field. The \<emph\>Row input cell\</emph\> and the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> fields are used to enter the reference to the corresponding cells of the formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149949				0	hi	दो वेरिएबल से गणना करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154808				0	hi	Consider columns A and B of the sample table above. You now want to vary not just the quantity produced annually, but also the selling price, and you are interested in the profit in each case.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149731				0	hi	Expand the table shown above. D2 through D11 contain the numbers 500, 1000 and so on, up to 5000. In E1 through H1 enter the numbers 8, 10, 15 and 20.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3152810				0	hi	दायरा  D1:H11 चुनें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153620				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple Operations\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149981				0	hi	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field, click cell B5.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	hi	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Row input cell\</emph\> field and click cell B1. This means that B1, the selling price, is the horizontally entered variable (with the values 8, 10, 15 and 20).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154049				0	hi	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> field and click in B4. This means that B4, the quantity, is the vertically entered variable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149141				0	hi	Close the dialog with OK. You see the profits for the different selling prices in the range E2:H11.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3155104				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12060000.xhp\" name=\"Multiple operations\"\>Multiple operations\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	सीएसवी फ़ाइलें आयात तथा निर्यात करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id892361				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>number series import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data series import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; tables as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; tables as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>delimited values and files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comma separated files and values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text file import and export\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>csv files;importing and exporting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; importing/exporting as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents; importing to spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening;text csv files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;as text csv\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10862				0	hi	\<variable id=\"csv_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/csv_files.xhp\"\>Opening and Saving Text CSV Files\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10880				0	hi	Comma Separated Values (CSV) is a text file format that you can use to exchange data from a database or a spreadsheet between applications. Each line in a Text CSV file represents a record in the database, or a row in a spreadsheet. Each field in a database record or cell in a spreadsheet row is usually separated by a comma. However, you can use other characters to delimit a field, such as a tabulator character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10886				0	hi	If the field or cell contains a comma, the field or cell \<emph\>must\</emph\> be enclosed by single quotes (') or double quotes (").				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10890				0	hi	To Open a Text CSV File in Calc				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10897				0	hi	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1089F				0	hi	सीएसवी फ़ाइल को ढूंढें जिसे आप खोलना चाहते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A2				0	hi	यदि फ़ाइल में *.csv एक्सटेंशन है, फ़ाइल चुनें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A5				0	hi	If the CSV file has another extension, select the file, and then select "Text CSV" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File type\</item\> box				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082D				0	hi	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Open\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	hi	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Import\</item\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108B1				0	hi	पाठ को स्तम्भों में विभाजित करने के विकल्पों को निर्धारित करें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108BB				0	hi	You can preview the layout of the imported data at the bottom of the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Import\</item\> dialog. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_id8444166				0	hi	Right-click a column in the preview to set the format or to hide the column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E2				0	hi	Check the text delimiter box that matches the character used as text delimiter in the file. In case of an unlisted delimiter, type the character into the input box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C5				0	hi	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FA				0	hi	शीट को पाठ सीएसवी फ़ाइल में सहेजने के लिए				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FC				0	hi	When you export a spreadsheet to CSV format, only the data on the current sheet is saved. All other information, including formulas and formatting, is lost.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10901				0	hi	कॅल्क शीट खोलें जिसे आप पाठ सीएसवी फ़ाइल के रूप में सहेजना चाहते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AF				0	hi	सिर्फ वर्तमान शीट निर्यात किया जा सकता है.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10905				0	hi	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Save as\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10915				0	hi	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File name\</item\> box, enter a name for the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1090D				0	hi	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File type\</item\> box, select "Text CSV".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DD				0	hi	पाठ CSV फ़ाइल के लिए क्षेत्र विकल्प सेट करें (वैकल्पिक).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091C				0	hi	Select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit filter settings\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107ED				0	hi	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Export of text files\</item\> dialog, select the options that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F4				0	hi	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FC				0	hi	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Save\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
