helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091B				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Add\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10922				0	hi	छपाई दायरा क्लीयर करन के लिए				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10929				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Remove\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10953				0	hi	छपाई दायरा संपादित करने के लिए पृष्ठ ब्रेक पूर्वावलोकन इस्तेमाल करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093E				0	hi	In the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, print ranges as well as page break regions are outlined by a blue border and contain a centered page number in gray. Nonprinting areas have a gray background.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143				0	hi	To define a new page break region, drag the border to a new location. When you define a new page break region, an automatic page break is replaced by a manual page break.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10930				0	hi	छपाई दायरा संपादित करने व देखने के लिए				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10937				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082A				0	hi	To change the default zoom factor of the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, double click the percentage value on the \<emph\>Status\</emph\> bar, and select a new zoom factor.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10836				0	hi	छपाई का दायरा संपादित करें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10944				0	hi	छपाई क्षेत्रसीमा का आकार बदलने के लिए, क्षेत्रसीमा के किनारा को किसी नए स्थान पर खींचें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_id3151075				0	hi	To delete a manual page break that is contained in a print range, drag the border of the page break outside of the print range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10948				0	hi	किसी छपाई क्षेत्रसीमा को क्लीयर करने के लिए, क्षेत्र सीमा के किनारे को दूसरे किनारे पर खींच लाएँ.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10862				0	hi	To exit the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN109CF				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\"\>Editing Print Ranges\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	छपाई के लिए पृष्ठों की संख्या निर्धारित करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153194				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheet counts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing sheet counts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page breaks; spreadsheet preview\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>previews;page breaks for printing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153194				0	hi	\<variable id=\"print_exact\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_exact.xhp\" name=\"Defining Number of Pages for Printing\"\>Defining Number of Pages for Printing\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	hi	If a sheet is too large for a single printed page, $[officename] Calc will print the current sheet evenly divided over several pages. Since the automatic page break does not always take place in the optimal position, you can define the page distribution yourself.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155				0	hi	Go to the sheet to be printed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	hi	You will see the automatic distribution of the sheet across the print pages. The automatically created print ranges are indicated by dark blue lines, and the user-defined ones by light blue lines. The page breaks (line breaks and column breaks) are marked as black lines.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578				0	hi	You can move the blue lines with the mouse. You will find further options in the Context menu, including adding an additional print range, removing the scaling and inserting additional manual line and column breaks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	पता तथा संदर्भ, सापेक्ष तथा निरपेक्ष				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156423				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>addressing; relative and absolute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; absolute/relative\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>absolute addresses in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative addresses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>absolute references in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; to cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; references\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	hi	\<variable id=\"relativ_absolut_ref\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/relativ_absolut_ref.xhp\" name=\"Addresses and References, Absolute and Relative\"\>Addresses and References, Absolute and Relative\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163712				0	hi	सापेक्ष एड्रेसिंग				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	hi	The cell in column A, row 1 is addressed as A1. You can address a range of adjacent cells by first entering the coordinates of the upper left cell of the area, then a colon followed by the coordinates of the lower right cell. For example, the square formed by the first four cells in the upper left corner is addressed as A1:B2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730				0	hi	By addressing an area in this way, you are making a relative reference to A1:B2. Relative here means that the reference to this area will be adjusted automatically when you copy the formulas.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149377				0	hi	निरपेक्ष एड्रेसिंग				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3154943				0	hi	Absolute references are the opposite of relative addressing. A dollar sign is placed before each letter and number in an absolute reference, for example, $A$1:$B$2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	hi	$[officename] can convert the current reference, in which the cursor is positioned in the input line, from relative to absolute and vice versa by pressing Shift +F4. If you start with a relative address such as A1, the first time you press this key combination, both row and column are set to absolute references ($A$1). The second time, only the row (A$1), and the third time, only the column ($A1). If you press the key combination once more, both column and row references are switched back to relative (A1)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	hi	$[officename] Calc shows the references to a formula. If, for example you click the formula =SUM(A1:C5;D15:D24) in a cell, the two referenced areas in the sheet will be highlighted in color. For example, the formula component "A1:C5" may be in blue and the cell range in question bordered in the same shade of blue. The next formula component "D15:D24" can be marked in red in the same way.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154704				0	hi	सापेक्ष तथा निरपेक्ष संदर्भों को कब-कब इस्तेमाल करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3147346				0	hi	What distinguishes a relative reference? Assume you want to calculate in cell E1 the sum of the cells in range A1:B2. The formula to enter into E1 would be: =SUM(A1:B2). If you later decide to insert a new column in front of column A, the elements you want to add would then be in B1:C2 and the formula would be in F1, not in E1. After inserting the new column, you would therefore have to check and correct all formulas in the sheet, and possibly in other sheets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	hi	Fortunately, $[officename] does this work for you. After having inserted a new column A, the formula =SUM(A1:B2) will be automatically updated to =SUM(B1:C2). Row numbers will also be automatically adjusted when a new row 1 is inserted. Absolute and relative references are always adjusted in $[officename] Calc whenever the referenced area is moved. But be careful if you are copying a formula since in that case only the relative references will be adjusted, not the absolute references.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3145791				0	hi	Absolute references are used when a calculation refers to one specific cell in your sheet. If a formula that refers to exactly this cell is copied relatively to a cell below the original cell, the reference will also be moved down if you did not define the cell coordinates as absolute.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3147005				0	hi	Aside from when new rows and columns are inserted, references can also change when an existing formula referring to particular cells is copied to another area of the sheet. Assume you entered the formula =SUM(A1:A9) in row 10. If you want to calculate the sum for the adjacent column to the right, simply copy this formula to the cell to the right. The copy of the formula in column B will be automatically adjusted to =SUM(B1:B9).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	Editing Pivot Tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148663				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; editing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148663				0	hi	\<variable id=\"datapilot_edittable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_edittable.xhp\" name=\"Editing Pivot Tables\"\>Editing Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	hi	Click one of the buttons in the pivot table and hold the mouse button down. A special symbol will appear next to the mouse pointer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	hi	By dragging the button to a different position in the same row you can alter the order of the columns. If you drag a button to the left edge of the table into the row headings area, you can change a column into a row.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id1648915				0	hi	In the Pivot Table dialog, you can drag a button to the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area to create a button and a listbox on top of the pivot table. The listbox can be used to filter the pivot table by the contents of the selected item. You can use drag-and-drop within the pivot table to use another page field as a filter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	hi	To remove a button from the table, just drag it out of the pivot table. Release the mouse button when the mouse pointer positioned within the sheet has become a 'not allowed' icon. The button is deleted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	hi	To edit the pivot table, click a cell inside the pivot table and open the context menu. In the context menu you find the command \<emph\>Edit Layout\</emph\>, which displays the \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\> dialog for the current pivot table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id2666096				0	hi	In the pivot table, you can use drag-and-drop or cut/paste commands to rearrange the order of data fields.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id266609688				0	hi	You can assign custom display names to fields, field members, subtotals (with some restrictions), and grand totals inside pivot tables. A custom display name is assigned to an item by overwriting the original name with another name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	डाटा एकत्र करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>consolidating data\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>ranges; combining\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>combining;cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; combining\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>data; merging cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>merging;data ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791				0	hi	\<variable id=\"consolidate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/consolidate.xhp\" name=\"Consolidating Data\"\>Consolidating Data\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153191				0	hi	During consolidation, the contents of the cells from several sheets will be combined in one place.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	hd_id892056				0	hi	To Combine Cell Contents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	hi	उस दस्तावेज़ को खोलें जिसमें एकत्र किए जाने वाले कक्ष के दायरे हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154513				0	hi	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Consolidate\</item\> to open the \<emph\>Consolidate\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	hi	From the \<emph\>Source data area\</emph\> box select a source cell range to consolidate with other areas.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149209				0	hi	If the range is not named, click in the field next to the \<emph\>Source data area\</emph\>. A blinking text cursor appears. Type a reference for the first source data range or select the range with the mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	hi	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to insert the selected range in the \<emph\>Consolidation areas\</emph\> field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153816				0	hi	Select additional ranges and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> after each selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3157983				0	hi	Specify where you want to display the result by selecting a target range from the \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150215				0	hi	If the target range is not named, click in the field next to \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> and enter the reference of the target range. Alternatively, you can select the range using the mouse or position the cursor in the top left cell of the target range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153813				0	hi	Select a function from the \<emph\>Function\</emph\> box. The function specifies how the values of the consolidation ranges are linked. The "Sum" function is the default setting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149315				0	hi	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to consolidate the ranges.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DE				0	hi	अतिरिक्त विन्यास				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147250				0	hi	Click \<emph\>More\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Consolidate\</emph\> dialog to display additional settings:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3156400				0	hi	Select \<emph\>Link to source data\</emph\> to insert the formulas that generate the results in the target range, rather than the actual results. If you link the data, any values modified in the source range are automatically updated in the target range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150538				0	hi	The corresponding cell references in the target range are inserted in consecutive rows, which are automatically ordered and then hidden from view. Only the final result, based on the selected function, is displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149945				0	hi	Under \<emph\>Consolidate by\</emph\>, select either \<emph\>Row labels\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column labels\</emph\> if the cells of the source data range are not to be consolidated corresponding to the identical position of the cell in the range, but instead according to a matching row label or column label.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871				0	hi	To consolidate by row labels or column labels, the label must be contained in the selected source ranges.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150478				0	hi	The text in the labels must be identical, so that rows or columns can be accurately matched. If the row or column label does not match any that exist in the target range, it will be appended as a new row or column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147468				0	hi	The data from the consolidation ranges and target range will be saved when you save the document. If you later open a document in which consolidation has been defined, this data will again be available.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153039				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12070000.xhp\" name=\"Data - Consolidate\"\>Data - Consolidate\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	सूत्र के द्वारा फ़ॉर्मेट निर्दिष्ट करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145673				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>formats; assigning by formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell formats; assigning by formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>STYLE function example\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell styles;assigning by formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas;assigning cell formats\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145673	13			0	hi	\<variable id=\"cellstyle_by_formula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_by_formula.xhp\" name=\"Assigning Formats by Formula\"\>Assigning Formats by Formula\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	hi	The STYLE() function can be added to an existing formula in a cell. For example, together with the CURRENT function, you can color a cell depending on its value. The formula =...+STYLE(IF(CURRENT()>3; "Red"; "Green")) applies the cell style "Red" to cells if the value is greater than 3, otherwise the cell style "Green" is applied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385				0	hi	If you would like to apply a formula to all cells in a selected area, you can use the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find & Replace\</item\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	hi	सभी वांछित कक्षों को चुनें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	hi	Select the menu command \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767	18			0	hi	For the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for\</item\> term, enter: .\<item type=\"literal\"\>*\</item\>            				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153770				0	hi	".*" is a regular expression that designates the contents of the current cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143	20			0	hi	Enter the following formula in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Replace with\</item\> field: \<item type=\"literal\"\>=&+STYLE(IF(CURRENT()>3;"Red";"Green"))\</item\>            				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	hi	The "&" symbol designates the current contents of the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> field. The line must begin with an equal sign, since it is a formula. It is assumed that the cell styles "Red" and "Green" already exist.				20200411 15:09:53
