helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	Using Scenarios				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149664				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>scenarios; creating/editing/deleting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening;scenarios\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;scenarios in Navigator\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	hi	\<variable id=\"scenario\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/scenario.xhp\" name=\"Using Scenarios\"\>Using Scenarios\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	hi	A $[officename] Calc scenario is a set of cell values that can be used within your calculations. You assign a name to every scenario on your sheet. Define several scenarios on the same sheet, each with some different values in the cells. Then you can easily switch the sets of cell values by their name and immediately observe the results. Scenarios are a tool to test out "what-if" questions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149255				0	hi	स्वयं अपने लिए सीनारियो बनाना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704	16			0	hi	To create a scenario, select all the cells that provide the data for the scenario. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	hi	Select the cells that contain the values that will change between scenarios. To select multiple cells, hold down the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\</item\>key as you click each cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3150364				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Scenarios\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Create Scenario\</emph\> dialog appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	hi	Enter a name for the new scenario and leave the other fields unchanged with their default values. Close the dialog with OK. Your new scenario is automatically activated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149664				0	hi	Using Scenarios				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	hi	Scenarios can be selected in the Navigator:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752	12			0	hi	Open the Navigator with the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id1593676\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_navigator.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1593676\"\>Navigator icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the Standard bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764	13			0	hi	Click the \<emph\>Scenarios\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id7617114\" src=\"sc/res/imglst/navipi/na07.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7617114\"\>Scenarios icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	hi	In the Navigator, you see the defined scenarios with the comments that were entered when the scenarios were created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id1243629				0	hi	Double-click a scenario name in the Navigator to apply that scenario to the current sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id9044770				0	hi	To delete a scenario, right-click the name in the Navigator and choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3674123				0	hi	To edit a scenario, right-click the name in the Navigator and choose \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3424481				0	hi	To hide the border of a set of cells that are part of a scenario, open the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog for each scenario that affects the cells and clear the Display border checkbox. Hiding the border also removes the listbox on the sheet where you can choose the scenarios.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	hi	If you want to know which values in the scenario affect other values, choose \<emph\>Tools - Detective - Trace Dependents\</emph\>. You see arrows to the cells that are directly dependent on the current cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06050000.xhp\" name=\"Creating Scenarios\"\>Creating Scenarios\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	Updating Pivot Tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150792				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; refreshing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recalculating;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	hi	\<variable id=\"datapilot_updatetable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_updatetable.xhp\" name=\"Updating Pivot Tables\"\>Updating Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	hi	If the data of the source sheet has been changed, $[officename] recalculates the pivot table. To recalculate the table, choose \<emph\>Data - Pivot Table - Refresh\</emph\>. Do the same after you have imported an Excel pivot table into $[officename] Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	गोल सीक लागू करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>goal seeking;example\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>equations in goal seek\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;variables in equations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variables;calculating equations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples;goal seek\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	hi	\<variable id=\"goalseek\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/goalseek.xhp\" name=\"Applying Goal Seek\"\>Applying Goal Seek\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	hi	With the help of Goal Seek you can calculate a value that, as part of a formula, leads to the result you specify for the formula. You thus define the formula with several fixed values and one variable value and the result of the formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153966				0	hi	गोल सीक उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150871				0	hi	To calculate annual interest (I), create a table with the values for the capital (C), number of years (n), and interest rate (i). The formula is:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596				0	hi	I = C * n* i				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	hi	Let us assume that the interest rate \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> of 7.5% and the number of years \<item type=\"literal\"\>n\</item\> (1) will remain constant. However, you want to know how much the investment capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> would have to be modified in order to attain a particular return \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\>. For this example, calculate how much capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> would be required if you want an annual return of $15,000.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	hi	Enter each of the values for Capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> (an arbitrary value like \<item type=\"literal\"\>$100,000\</item\>), number of years \<item type=\"literal\"\>n \</item\>(\<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\>), and interest rate \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> (\<item type=\"literal\"\>7.5%\</item\>) in one cell each. Enter the formula to calculate the interest \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\> in another cell. Instead of \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\>, \<item type=\"literal\"\>n\</item\>, and \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/relativ_absolut_ref.xhp\"\>reference to the cell\</link\> with the corresponding value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	hi	Place the cursor in the cell containing the interest \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\>, and choose \<emph\>Tools - Goal Seek\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Goal Seek\</emph\> dialog appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	hi	The correct cell is already entered in the field \<emph\>Formula Cell\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	hi	Place the cursor in the field \<emph\>Variable Cell\</emph\>. In the sheet, click in the cell that contains the value to be changed, in this example it is the cell with the capital value \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150369				0	hi	Enter the expected result of the formula in the \<emph\>Target Value\</emph\> text box. In this example, the value is 15,000. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3146978				0	hi	A dialog appears informing you that the Goal Seek was successful. Click \<emph\>Yes\</emph\> to enter the result in the cell with the variable value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3149409				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Goal Seek\"\>Goal Seek\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	बहुल शीट में नक़ल करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>copying;values, to multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;values in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data;inserting in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>sheets; simultaneous multiple filling\</bookmark_value\> 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456	3			0	hi	\<variable id=\"edit_multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/edit_multitables.xhp\" name=\"Copying to Multiple Sheets\"\>Copying to Multiple Sheets\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	hi	In $[officename] Calc, you can insert values, text or formulas that are simultaneously copied to other selected sheets of your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	hi	Select all desired sheets by holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key and clicking the corresponding register tabs that are still gray at the bottom margin of the workspace. All selected register tabs are now white.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	hi	You can use Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up or Page Down to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435				0	hi	Now when you insert values, text or formulas into the active sheet, they will also appear in the identical positions in the other selected sheets. For example, data entered in cell A1 of the active sheet is automatically entered into cell A1 of any other seleted sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	संख्या को दशमलव के साथ फ़ॉर्मेट करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145367				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>numbers;formatting decimals\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; numbers in tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; number formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defaults; number formats in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>decimal places;formatting numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;numbers with decimals\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;adding/deleting decimal places\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number formats; adding/deleting decimal places in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting; decimal places\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>decimal places; adding/deleting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145367				0	hi	\<variable id=\"format_value\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_value.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Numbers With Decimals\"\>Formatting Numbers With Decimals\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	hi	Enter a number into the sheet, for example, 1234.5678. This number will be displayed in the default number format, with two decimal places. You will see 1234.57 when you confirm the entry. Only the display in the document will be rounded off; internally, the number retains all four decimal places after the decimal point.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012				0	hi	संख्या को दशमलव के साथ फ़ॉर्मेट करने के लिए:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	hi	Set the cursor at the number and choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> to start the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	hi	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab you will see a selection of predefined number formats. In the bottom right in the dialog you will see a preview of how your current number would look if you were to give it a particular format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3155766				0	hi	\<image id=\"img_id3149021\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_numberformatincdecimals.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149021\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3149256				0	hi	If you only want to modify the number of the decimal places displayed, the easiest method is to use the \<emph\>Number Format: Add Decimal Place\</emph\> or \<emph\>Number Format: Delete Decimal Place\</emph\> icons on the Formatting Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
