helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153969				0	hi	\<variable id=\"matrixformula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/matrixformula.xhp\" name=\"Entering Matrix Formulas\"\>Entering Matrix Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	hi	The following is an example of how you can enter a matrix formula, without going into the details of matrix functions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	hi	Assume you have entered 10 numbers in Columns A and B (A1:A10 and B1:B10), and would like to calculate the sum of each row in Column C.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321				0	hi	Using the mouse, select the range C1:C10, in which the results are to be displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	hi	 F2 दबाएँ  या सूत्र पट्टी में इनपुट लाइन पर क्लिक करें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	hi	बराबर चिह्न (=) प्रविष्ट करें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	hi	दायरा A1:A10 चुनें, जो योग सूत्र के प्रथम मूल्यों को रखता है.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3144767				0	hi	न्यूमेरिकल कुंजीपट में (+) कुंजी दबाएँ				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	hi	द्वितीय स्तम्भ के कक्षों B1:B10 में से संख्या चुनें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150716				0	hi	End the input with the matrix key combination: Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	hi	The matrix area is automatically protected against modifications, such as deleting rows or columns. It is, however, possible to edit any formatting, such as the cell background.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	भिन्न प्रविष्ट करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155411				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>fractions; entering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; entering fractions \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;fractions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411				0	hi	\<variable id=\"fraction_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/fraction_enter.xhp\" name=\"Entering Fractions \"\>Entering Fractions \</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	hi	यदि आप किसी कक्ष में भिन्न संख्या प्रविष्ट करते हैं और इसका इस्तेमाल गणना के लिए करते हैं:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155133				0	hi	Enter "0 1/5" in a cell (without the quotation marks) and press the input key. In the input line above the spreadsheet you will see the value 0.2, which is used for the calculation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	hi	If you enter "0 1/2" AutoCorrect causes the three characters 1, / and 2 to be replaced by a single character. The same applies to 1/4 and 3/4. This replacement is defined in \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options - Options\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145367	44			0	hi	If you want to see multi-digit fractions such as "1/10", you must change the cell format to the multi-digit fraction view. Open the context menu of the cell, and choose \<emph\>Format cells. \</emph\>Select "Fraction" from the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> field, and then select "-1234 10/81". You can then enter fractions such as 12/31 or 12/32 - the fractions are, however, automatically reduced, so that in the last example you would see 3/8.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	कक्षों को नाम देना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147434				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>cells; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>names; defining for cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>values; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>constants definition\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>variables; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell ranges; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;names for cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>addressing; by defined names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell names; defining/addressing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references; by defined names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>allowed cell names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>renaming;cells\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434				0	hi	\<variable id=\"value_with_name\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/value_with_name.xhp\" name=\"Naming Cells\"\>Naming Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	hd_id4391918				0	hi	Allowed names				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id2129581				0	hi	Names in Calc can contain letters, numeric characters, and some special characters. Names must start with a letter or an underline character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id1120029				0	hi	Allowed special characters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3362224				0	hi	underline (_) 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id4891506				0	hi	period (.) - allowed within a name, but not as first or last character				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id2816553				0	hi	blank ( ) - allowed within a name, but not as first or last character, and not for a cell range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id328989				0	hi	Names must not be the same as cell references. For example, the name A1 is invalid because A1 is a cell reference to the top left cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id32898987				0	hi	Names must not start with the letter R followed by a number. See the ADDRESS function for more information.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id4769737				0	hi	Names for cell ranges must not include blanks. Blanks are allowed within names for single cells, sheets and documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	hd_id1226233				0	hi	Naming cells and formulas				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id5489364				0	hi	A good way of making the references to cells and cell ranges in formulas legible is to give the ranges names. For example, you can name the range A1:B2 \<emph\>Start\</emph\>. You can then write a formula such as "=SUM(Start)". Even after you insert or delete rows or columns, $[officename] still correctly assigns the ranges identified by name. Range names must not contain any spaces.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id953398				0	hi	For example, it is much easier to read a formula for sales tax if you can write "= Amount * Tax_rate" instead of "= A5 * B12". In this case, you would name cell A5 "Amount" and cell B12 "Tax_rate."				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id4889675				0	hi	Use the \<emph\>Define Names\</emph\> dialog to define names for formulas or parts of formulas you need more often. In order to specify range names,				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3153954				0	hi	Select a cell or range of cells, then choose \<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Define Names\</emph\> dialog appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	hi	Type the name of the selected area in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> field. Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>. The newly defined name appears in the list below. Click OK to close the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id5774101				0	hi	You can also name other cell ranges in this dialog by entering the name in the field and then selecting the respective cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942				0	hi	यदि आप सूत्र में नाम प्रविष्ट करते हैं, तो प्रथम कुछ अक्षर भरने पर आप सम्पूर्ण नाम को संकेत रूप में देखेंगे. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	hi	टिप से नाम स्वीकार करने के लिए एंटर कुंजी दबाएँ.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	hi	If more than one name starts with the same characters, you can scroll through all the names using the Tab key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04070100.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Names - Define\"\>Insert - Names - Define\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	Filtering Cell Ranges 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153541				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>cell ranges;applying/removing filters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>filtering;cell ranges/database ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>database ranges;applying/removing filters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>removing;cell range filters\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153541				0	hi	\<variable id=\"database_filter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_filter.xhp\" name=\"Filtering Cell Ranges\"\>Filtering Cell Ranges\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069				0	hi	You can use several filters to filter cell ranges in spreadsheets. A standard filter uses the options that you specify to filter the data. An AutoFilter filters data according to a specific value or string. An advanced filter uses filter criteria from specified cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	hi	To Apply a Standard Filter to a Cell Range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398				0	hi	Click in a cell range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10693				0	hi	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - Standard Filter\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	hi	In the \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> dialog, specify the filter options that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A5				0	hi	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143				0	hi	रेकॉर्ड जो फ़िल्टर मापदण्ड से मेल खाते हैं जो आपने चुने हैं वे दिखाए गए हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	hi	To Apply an AutoFilter to a Cell Range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	hi	Click in a cell range or a database range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id9303872				0	hi	If you want to apply multiple AutoFilters to the same sheet, you must first define database ranges, then apply the AutoFilters to the database ranges.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	hi	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DB				0	hi	An arrow button is added to the head of each column in the database range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	hi	Click the arrow button in the column that contains the value or string that you want to set as the filter criteria.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	hi	मूल्य या स्ट्रिंग चुनें जिसे आप फ़िल्टर मापदण्ड के रूप में इस्तेमाल करना चाहते हैं. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074C				0	hi	रेकॉर्ड जो फ़िल्टर मापदण्ड से मेल खाते हैं जो आपने चुने हैं वे दिखाए गए हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	hi	To Remove a Filter From a Cell Range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075C				0	hi	Click in a filtered cell range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EC				0	hi	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - Remove Filter\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id4525284				0	hi	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Defining_a_Data_Range\"\>Wiki page about defining a data range\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	Handling of Empty Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146799				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>empty cells;handling of\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id1502121				0	hi	\<variable id=\"empty_cells\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/05/empty_cells.xhp\"\>Handling of Empty Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id8266853				0	hi	In older versions of the software, empty cells were forced to numeric 0 in some contexts and to empty string in others, except in direct comparison where =A1=0 and =A1="" both resulted in TRUE if A1 was empty. Emptiness now is inherited until used, so both =VLOOKUP(...)=0 and =VLOOKUP(...)="" give TRUE if the lookup resulted in an empty cell being returned. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id2733542				0	hi	A simple reference to an empty cell is still displayed as numeric 0 but is not necessarily of type numeric anymore, so also comparisons with the referencing cell work as expected. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4238715				0	hi	For the following examples, A1 contains a number, B1 is empty, C1 contains the reference to B1:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id8277230				0	hi	A1: 1 B1: <empty> C1: =B1 (displays 0)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4086428				0	hi	=B1=0 => TRUE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id9024628				0	hi	=B1="" => TRUE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3067110				0	hi	=C1=0 => TRUE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id8841822				0	hi	=C1="" => TRUE (previously was FALSE)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4077578				0	hi	=ISNUMBER(B1) => FALSE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id9094515				0	hi	=ISNUMBER(C1) => FALSE (previously was TRUE)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id396740				0	hi	=ISNUMBER(VLOOKUP(1;A1:C1;2)) => FALSE (B1)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3859675				0	hi	=ISNUMBER(VLOOKUP(1;A1:C1;3)) => FALSE (C1, previously was TRUE)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id402233				0	hi	=ISTEXT(B1) => FALSE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id1623889				0	hi	=ISTEXT(C1) => FALSE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id7781914				0	hi	=ISTEXT(VLOOKUP(1;A1:C1;2)) => FALSE (B1, previously was TRUE)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id300912				0	hi	=ISTEXT(VLOOKUP(1;A1:C1;3)) => FALSE (C1)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id9534592				0	hi	=ISBLANK(B1) => TRUE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4969328				0	hi	=ISBLANK(C1) => FALSE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id9635914				0	hi	=ISBLANK(VLOOKUP(1;A1:C1;2)) => TRUE (B1, previously was FALSE)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id2476577				0	hi	=ISBLANK(VLOOKUP(1;A1:C1;3)) => FALSE (C1)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4217047				0	hi	Note that Microsoft Excel behaves different and always returns a number as the result of a reference to an empty cell or a formula cell with the result of an empty cell. For example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id2629474				0	hi	A1: <empty>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id8069704				0	hi	B1: =A1 => displays 0, but is just a reference to an empty cell				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4524674				0	hi	=ISNUMBER(A1) => FALSE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4396801				0	hi	=ISTEXT(A1) => FALSE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id5293740				0	hi	=A1=0 => TRUE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id7623828				0	hi	=A1="" => TRUE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id2861720				0	hi	=ISNUMBER(B1) => FALSE (MS-Excel: TRUE)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id9604480				0	hi	=ISTEXT(B1) => FALSE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id2298959				0	hi	=B1=0 => TRUE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id4653767				0	hi	=B1="" => TRUE (MS-Excel: FALSE)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id8801538				0	hi	C1: =VLOOKUP(...) with empty cell result => displays empty (MS-Excel: displays 0)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\05\empty_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id6746421				0	hi	=ISNUMBER(VLOOKUP(...)) => FALSE				20200411 15:09:53
