helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481	104			0	hi	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=CHITEST(A1:A6;B1:B6)\</item\> equals 0.02. This is the probability which suffices the observed data of the theoretical Chi-square distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148690				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>CHIDIST function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148690				0	hi	CHIDIST				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156338				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_CHIVERT\"\>Returns the probability value from the indicated Chi square that a hypothesis is confirmed.\</ahelp\> CHIDIST compares the Chi square value to be given for a random sample that is calculated from the sum of (observed value-expected value)^2/expected value for all values with the theoretical Chi square distribution and determines from this the probability of error for the hypothesis to be tested.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3151316				0	hi	जो प्रॉबेबिलिटी CHIDIST द्वारा निर्धारित की जाती है वह CHITEST द्वारा भी की जाती है.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155123				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3158439				0	hi	CHIDIST(Number; DegreesFreedom)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3148675	110			0	hi	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the chi-square value of the random sample used to determine the error probability.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3155615	111			0	hi	            \<emph\>DegreesFreedom\</emph\> are the degrees of freedom of the experiment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146787				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3145774	113			0	hi	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=CHIDIST(13.27; 5)\</item\> equals 0.02.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3156141				0	hi	If the Chi square value of the random sample is 13.27 and if the experiment has 5 degrees of freedom, then the hypothesis is assured with a probability of error of 2%.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id0119200902231887				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>CHISQDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chi-square distribution\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id0119200901583452				0	hi	CHISQDIST				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200901583471				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Returns the value of the probability density function or the cumulative distribution function for the chi-square distribution.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id0119200902395520				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902395679				0	hi	CHISQDIST(Number; Degrees Of Freedom; Cumulative)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id011920090239564				0	hi	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number for which the function is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902395660				0	hi	            \<emph\>Degrees Of Freedom\</emph\> is the degrees of freedom for the chi-square function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200902395623				0	hi	            \<emph\>Cumulative\</emph\> (optional): 0 or False calculates the probability density function. Other values or True or omitted calculates the cumulative distribution function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150603				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>EXPONDIST function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>exponential distributions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150603				0	hi	EXPONDIST				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149563				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_EXPONVERT\"\>Returns the exponential distribution.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153789				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150987				0	hi	EXPONDIST(Number; Lambda; C)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154663	119			0	hi	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value of the function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154569	120			0	hi	            \<emph\>Lambda\</emph\> is the parameter value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3147332	121			0	hi	            \<emph\>C\</emph\> is a logical value that determines the form of the function. \<emph\>C = 0\</emph\> calculates the density function, and \<emph\>C = 1\</emph\> calculates the distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146133				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150357	123			0	hi	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=EXPONDIST(3;0.5;1)\</item\> returns 0.78.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	AutoInput				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	bm_id2486037				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>entering entries with AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>capital letters;AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148492				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"AutoInput\"\>AutoInput\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150793				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:AutoComplete\"\>Switches the AutoInput function on and off, which automatically completes entries, based on other entries in the same column.\</ahelp\> The column is scanned up to a maximum of 2000 cells or 200 different strings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	hi	कम्प्लीशन पाठ उभारा गया है.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065D				0	hi	To accept the completion, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> or a cursor key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10665				0	hi	To append text or to edit the completion, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F2\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066D				0	hi	To view more completions, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> to scroll forward, or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> to scroll backward.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10679				0	hi	To see a list of all available AutoInput text items for the current column, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+D.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	hi	When typing formulas using characters that match previous entries, a Help tip will appear listing the last ten functions used from \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>, from all defined range names, from all database range names, and from the content of all label ranges.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	hi	AutoInput is case-sensitive. If, for example, you have written "Total" in a cell, you cannot enter "total" in another cell of the same column without first deactivating AutoInput.				20200411 15:09:53
