helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158446				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>MUNIT function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158446				0	hi	MUNIT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154121				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_EINHEITSMATRIX\"\>Returns the unitary square array of a certain size.\</ahelp\> The unitary array is a square array where the main diagonal elements equal 1 and all other array elements are equal to 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155123				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3156271				0	hi	MUNIT(Dimensions)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3159390				0	hi	\<emph\>Dimensions\</emph\> refers to the size of the array unit.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C9B				0	hi	ऐरे फ़ंक्शन को इस्तेमाल करने के लिए सामान्य परिचय आपको इस पृष्ठ के शीर्ष में मिलेगा.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156162				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150949				0	hi	स्प्रेडशीट के भीतर वर्गाकार दायरा चुनें, उदाहरण के लिए,  A1 से E5.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3151260				0	hi	Without deselecting the range, select the MUNIT function. Mark the \<emph\>Array\</emph\> check box. Enter the desired dimensions for the array unit, in this case \<item type=\"input\"\>5\</item\>, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150403				0	hi	You can also enter the \<item type=\"input\"\>=Munit(5)\</item\> formula in the last cell of the selected range (E5), and press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Shift+Command+Enter\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Shift+Ctrl+Enter\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3156143				0	hi	अब आप दायरा A1:E5 सहित इकाई ऐरे देख सकते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN10FA7				0	hi	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#moreontop\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159084				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>FREQUENCY function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159084				0	hi	FREQUENCY				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3145777				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_HAEUFIGKEIT\"\>Indicates the frequency distribution in a one-column-array.\</ahelp\> The function counts the number of values in the Data array that are within the values given by the Classes array.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153347				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155498				0	hi	FREQUENCY(Data; Classes)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154352				0	hi	\<emph\>Data\</emph\> represents the reference to the values to be counted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3148402				0	hi	\<emph\>Classes\</emph\> represents the array of the limit values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D71				0	hi	ऐरे फ़ंक्शन को इस्तेमाल करने के लिए सामान्य परिचय आपको इस पृष्ठ के शीर्ष में मिलेगा.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148981				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155904				0	hi	In the following table, column A lists unsorted measurement values. Column B contains the upper limit you entered for the classes into which you want to divide the data in column A. According to the limit entered in B1, the FREQUENCY function returns the number of measured values less than or equal to 5. As the limit in B2 is 10, the FREQUENCY function returns the second result as the number of measured values that are greater than 5 and less than or equal to 10. The text you entered in B6, ">25", is only for reference purposes.				20200411 15:09:53
