helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151180				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3156130	101			0	hi	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=TRIMMEAN(A1:A50; 0.1)\</item\> calculates the mean value of numbers in A1:A50, without taking into consideration the 5 percent of the values representing the highest values and the 5 percent of the values representing the lowest ones. The percentage numbers refer to the amount of the untrimmed mean value, not to the number of summands.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153216				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>ZTEST function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153216				0	hi	ZTEST				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3150758				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_GTEST\"\>Calculates the probability of observing a z-statistic greater than the one computed based on a sample.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150872				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3153274				0	hi	ZTEST(Data; Number; Sigma)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3156109	107			0	hi	            \<emph\>Data\</emph\> is the given sample, drawn from a normally distributed population.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3149977	108			0	hi	            \<emph\>mu\</emph\> is the known mean of the population.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3154740	109			0	hi	            \<emph\>Sigma\</emph\> (optional) is the known standard deviation of the population. If omitted, the standard deviation of the given sample is used.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372999				0	hi	See also the \<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Calc:_ZTEST_function\"\>Wiki page\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153623				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>HARMEAN function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>means;harmonic\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153623				0	hi	HARMEAN				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3155102				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_HARMITTEL\"\>Returns the harmonic mean of a data set.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146900				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3149287				0	hi	HARMEAN(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3154303	117			0	hi	            \<emph\>Number1,Number2,...Number30\</emph\> are up to 30 values or ranges, that can be used to calculate the harmonic mean.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159179				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3146093	120			0	hi	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=HARMEAN(23;46;69)\</item\> = 37.64. The harmonic mean of this random sample is thus 37.64				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152801				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>HYPGEOMDIST function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>sampling without replacement\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801				0	hi	HYPGEOMDIST				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3159341				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_HYPGEOMVERT\"\>Returns the hypergeometric distribution.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154697				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	hi	HYPGEOMDIST(X; NSample; Successes; NPopulation)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3154933	126			0	hi	            \<emph\>X\</emph\> is the number of results achieved in the random sample.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3153106	127			0	hi	            \<emph\>NSample\</emph\> is the size of the random sample.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3146992	128			0	hi	            \<emph\>Successes\</emph\> is the number of possible results in the total population.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3148826	129			0	hi	            \<emph\>NPopulation \</emph\>is the size of the total population.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150529				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3154904	131			0	hi	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=HYPGEOMDIST(2;2;90;100)\</item\> yields 0.81. If 90 out of 100 pieces of buttered toast fall from the table and hit the floor with the buttered side first, then if 2 pieces of buttered toast are dropped from the table, the probability is 81%, that both will strike buttered side first.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	Create Scenario				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156023				0	hi	Create Scenario				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	hi	\<variable id=\"szenariotext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ScenarioManager\"\>Defines a scenario for the selected sheet area.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10637				0	hi	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/guide/scenario.xhp#scenario\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156280				0	hi	दृश्य का नाम				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041	13			0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_SCENWIN_TOP\"\>Defines the name for the scenario. Use a clear and unique name so you can easily identify the scenario.\</ahelp\> You can also modify a scenario name in the Navigator through the \<emph\>Properties \</emph\>context menu command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153954				0	hi	टिप्पणी				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411	15			0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SC_SCENWIN_BOTTOM\"\>Specifies additional information about the scenario. This information will be displayed in the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\> when you click the \<emph\>Scenarios\</emph\> icon and select the desired scenario.\</ahelp\> You can also modify this information in the Navigator through the \<emph\>Properties \</emph\>context menu command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145273				0	hi	विन्यास				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153364				0	hi	This section is used to define some of the settings used in the scenario display.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145367				0	hi	किनारा दिखाएँ				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:LB_COLOR\"\>Highlights the scenario in your table with a border. The color for the border is specified in the field to the right of this option.\</ahelp\> The border will have a title bar displaying the name of the last scenario. The button on the right of the scenario border offers you an overview of all the scenarios in this area, if several have been defined. You can choose any of the scenarios from this list without restrictions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149582				0	hi	पीछे नक़ल करें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:CB_TWOWAY\"\>Copies the values of cells that you change into the active scenario. If you do not select this option, the scenario is not changed when you change cell values. The behavior of the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> setting depends on the cell protection, the sheet protection, and the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> settings.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149402				0	hi	पूरी शीट नक़ल करें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969	23			0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:CB_COPYALL\"\>Copies the entire sheet into an additional scenario sheet. \</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075A				0	hi	परिवर्तन रोकें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075E				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"sc:CheckBox:RID_SCDLG_NEWSCENARIO:CB_PROTECT\"\>Prevents changes to the active scenario. The behavior of the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> setting depends on the cell protection, the sheet protection, and the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> settings.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10778				0	hi	You can only change the scenario properties if the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> option is not selected and if the sheet is not protected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10780				0	hi	You can only edit cell values if the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> option is selected, if the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> is option is not selected, and if the cells are not protected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078C				0	hi	You can only change scenario cell values and write them back into the scenario if the \<emph\>Prevent changes\</emph\> option is not selected, if the \<emph\>Copy back\</emph\> option is selected, and if the cells are not protected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	फिर-से-गणना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157909				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>recalculating;all formulas in sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; recalculating manually\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell contents; recalculating\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157909				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Recalculate\"\>Recalculate\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Calculate\"\>Recalculates all changed formulas. If AutoCalculate is enabled, the Recalculate command applies only to formulas like RAND or NOW.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	par_id315475899				0	hi	Press F9 to recalculate. Press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F9 to recalculate all formulas in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150793				0	hi	After the document has been recalculated, the display is refreshed. All charts are also refreshed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06080000.xhp	0	help	par_id315475855				0	hi	The Add-In functions like RANDBETWEEN currently cannot respond to the Recalculate command or F9. Press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F9 to recalculate all formulas, including the Add-In functions.				20200411 15:09:53
