helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149198				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>XNPV function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149198				0	hi	XNPV				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153904				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_XNPV\"\>Calculates the capital value (net present value)for a list of payments which take place on different dates.\</ahelp\> The calculation is based on a 365 days per year basis, ignoring leap years.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN11138				0	hi	यदि भुगतान नियमित अंतराल पर होता है, तो एनपीवी फ़ंक्शन का इस्तेमाल करें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155323				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150117				0	hi	XNPV(Rate; Values; Dates)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153100				0	hi	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the internal rate of return for the payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155395				0	hi	\<emph\>Values\</emph\> and \<emph\>Dates\</emph\> refer to a series of payments and the series of associated date values. The first pair of dates defines the start of the payment plan. All other date values must be later, but need not be in any order. The series of values must contain at least one negative and one positive value (receipts and deposits)				20200411 15:09:53
