helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154569				0	hi	\<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is the number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150826				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148968				0	hi	A security is purchased on 2001-01-25; the date of maturity is 2001-11-15. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) what was the interest date prior to purchase?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149992				0	hi	=COUPPCD("2001-01-25"; "2001-11-15"; 2; 3) returns 2000-15-11.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150673				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>COUPNUM function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of coupons\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150673				0	hi	COUPNUM				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154350				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_COUPNUM\"\>Returns the number of coupons (interest payments) between the settlement date and the maturity date.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148400				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153200				0	hi	COUPNUM(Settlement; Maturity; Frequency; Basis)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3159406				0	hi	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155864				0	hi	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154720				0	hi	\<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is the number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149319				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3152460				0	hi	A security is purchased on 2001-01-25; the date of maturity is 2001-11-15. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) how many interest dates are there?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150640				0	hi	=COUPNUM("2001-01-25"; "2001-11-15"; 2; 3) returns 2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149339				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>IPMT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>periodic amortizement rates\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149339				0	hi	IPMT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154522				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZINSZ\"\>Calculates the periodic amortizement for an investment with regular payments and a constant interest rate.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153266				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151283				0	hi	IPMT(Rate; Period; NPer; PV; FV; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147313				0	hi	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145158				0	hi	\<emph\>Period\</emph\> is the period, for which the compound interest is calculated. Period=NPER if compound interest for the last period is calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147577				0	hi	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the total number of periods, during which annuity is paid.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156211				0	hi	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present cash value in sequence of payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151213				0	hi	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> (optional) is the desired value (future value) at the end of the periods.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154195				0	hi	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> is the due date for the periodic payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150102				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149438				0	hi	What is the interest rate during the fifth period (year) if the constant interest rate is 5% and the cash value is 15,000 currency units? The periodic payment is seven years.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150496				0	hi	\<item type=\"input\"\>=IPMT(5%;5;7;15000)\</item\> = -352.97 currency units. The compound interest during the fifth period (year) is 352.97 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151205				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;future values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>future values;constant interest rates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>FV function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151205				0	hi	FV				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154140				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZW\"\>Returns the future value of an investment based on periodic, constant payments and a constant interest rate (Future Value).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155178				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145215				0	hi	FV(Rate; NPer; Pmt; PV; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	hi	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156029				0	hi	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the total number of periods (payment period).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151322				0	hi	\<emph\>Pmt\</emph\> is the annuity paid regularly per period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145256				0	hi	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> (optional) is the (present) cash value of an investment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150999				0	hi	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) defines whether the payment is due at the beginning or the end of a period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN114D8				0	hi	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146800				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146813				0	hi	What is the value at the end of an investment if the interest rate is 4% and the payment period is two years, with a periodic payment of 750 currency units. The investment has a present value of 2,500 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149302				0	hi	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FV(4%;2;750;2500) \</item\>= -4234.00 currency units. The value at the end of the investment is 4234.00 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155912				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>FVSCHEDULE function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>future values;varying interest rates\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
