helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155802				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>COMBIN function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of combinations\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155802				0	hi	COMBIN				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3156172				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KOMBINATIONEN\"\>Returns the number of combinations for elements without repetition.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156193				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223				0	hi	COMBIN(Count1; Count2)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150313				0	hi	\<emph\>Count1\</emph\> is the number of items in the set.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153830				0	hi	\<emph\>Count2\</emph\> is the number of items to choose from the set.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6807458				0	hi	COMBIN returns the number of ordered ways to choose these items. For example if there are 3 items A, B and C in a set, you can choose 2 items in 3 different ways, namely AB, AC and BC.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7414471				0	hi	COMBIN implements the formula: Count1!/(Count2!*(Count1-Count2)!)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153171				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153517				0	hi	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COMBIN(3;2)\</item\> returns 3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150284				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>COMBINA function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of combinations with repetitions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150284				0	hi	COMBINA				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157894				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KOMBINATIONEN2\"\>Returns the number of combinations of a subset of items including repetitions.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145752				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145765				0	hi	COMBINA(Count1; Count2)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153372				0	hi	\<emph\>Count1\</emph\> is the number of items in the set.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155544				0	hi	\<emph\>Count2\</emph\> is the number of items to choose from the set.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1997131				0	hi	COMBINA returns the number of unique ways to choose these items, where the order of choosing is irrelevant, and repetition of items is allowed. For example if there are 3 items A, B and C in a set, you can choose 2 items in 6 different ways, namely AA, AB, AC, BB, BC and CC.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2052064				0	hi	COMBINA implements the formula: (Count1+Count2-1)! / (Count2!(Count1-1)!)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154584				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152904				0	hi	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COMBINA(3;2)\</item\> returns 6.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156086				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>TRUNC function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places;cutting off\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156086				0	hi	TRUNC				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157866				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KUERZEN\"\>Truncates a number by removing decimal places.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148499				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148511				0	hi	TRUNC(Number; Count)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150796				0	hi	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> with at most \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. Excess decimal places are simply removed, irrespective of sign.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150816				0	hi	\<item type=\"literal\"\>TRUNC(Number; 0)\</item\> behaves as \<item type=\"literal\"\>INT(Number)\</item\> for positive numbers, but effectively rounds towards zero for negative numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148548				0	hi	The \<emph\>visible\</emph\> decimal places of the result are specified in \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060500.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - Calculate\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152555				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152569				0	hi	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TRUNC(1.239;2)\</item\> returns 1.23. The 9 is lost.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7050080				0	hi	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TRUNC(-1.234999;3)\</item\> returns -1.234. All the 9s are lost.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153601				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>LN function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>natural logarithm\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153601				0	hi	LN				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154974				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LN\"\>Returns the natural logarithm based on the constant e of a number.\</ahelp\> The constant e has a value of approximately 2.71828182845904.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154993				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155284				0	hi	LN(Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155297				0	hi	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value whose natural logarithm is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153852				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153866				0	hi	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LN(3)\</item\> returns the natural logarithm of 3 (approximately 1.0986).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5747245				0	hi	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LN(EXP(321))\</item\> returns 321.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3109813				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>LOG function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>logarithms\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109813				0	hi	LOG				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3109841				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LOG\"\>Returns the logarithm of a number to the specified base.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144719				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144732				0	hi	LOG(Number; Base)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144746				0	hi	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value whose logarithm is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152840				0	hi	\<emph\>Base\</emph\> (optional) is the base for the logarithm calculation. If omitted, Base 10 is assumed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152860				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154429				0	hi	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LOG(10;3)\</item\> returns the logarithm to base 3 of 10 (approximately 2.0959).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5577562				0	hi	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LOG(7^4;7)\</item\> returns 4.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154187				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>LOG10 function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>base-10 logarithm\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
