helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152269				0	hi	Returns the (trigonometric) tangent of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, the angle in radians.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5752128				0	hi	To return the tangent of an angle in degrees, use the RADIANS function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152287				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152301				0	hi	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TAN(PI()/4) \</item\>returns 1, the tangent of PI/4 radians.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1804864				0	hi	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TAN(RADIANS(45))\</item\> returns 1, the tangent of 45 degrees.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3165434				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>TANH function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
