helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154908				0	hi	क्षेत्रसीमा में स्तम्भ लेबल हैं				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:BTN_HEADER\"\>Includes the column labels in the first row of a cell range.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155306				0	hi	Copy results to				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:ED_COPY_AREA\"\>Select the check box, and then select the cell range where you want to display the filter results.\</ahelp\> You can also select a named range from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145272				0	hi	रेग्युलर एक्सप्रेशन				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:BTN_REGEXP\"\>Allows you to use wildcards in the filter definition.\</ahelp\> For a list of the regular expressions that $[officename] supports, click \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100001.xhp\" name=\"here\"\>here\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	hi	If the \<emph\>Regular Expressions\</emph\> check box is selected, you can use regular expressions in the Value field if the Condition list box is set to '=' EQUAL or '<>' UNEQUAL. This also applies to the respective cells that you reference for an advanced filter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149958				0	hi	कोई नक़लें नहीं				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:BTN_UNIQUE\"\>Excludes duplicate rows in the list of filtered data.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154018				0	hi	फ़िल्टर मापदण्ड रखे रहें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149123				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_FILTER:BTN_DEST_PERS\"\>Select the \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> check box, and then specify the destination range where you want to display the filtered data. If this box is checked, the destination range remains linked to the source range. You must have defined the source range under \<emph\>Data - Define range\</emph\> as a database range.\</ahelp\> Following this, you can reapply the defined filter at any time as follows: click into the source range, then choose \<emph\>Data - Refresh Range\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	hi	डाटा क्षेत्रसीमा				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150042				0	hi	कक्ष क्षेत्रसीमा या कक्ष क्षेत्रसीमा का नाम जो आप फ़िल्टर करना चाहते हैं, प्रदर्शित करता है 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	WORKDAY				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149012				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>WORKDAY function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149012				0	hi	\<variable id=\"workday\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_workday.xhp\"\>WORKDAY\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149893				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_WORKDAY\"\> The result is a date number that can be formatted as a date. You then see the date of a day that is a certain number of \<emph\>workdays\</emph\> away from the \<emph\>start date\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146944				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154844				0	hi	WORKDAY(StartDate; Days; Holidays)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3147469				0	hi	\<emph\>StartDate\</emph\> is the date from when the calculation is carried out. If the start date is a workday, the day is included in the calculation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3153038				0	hi	\<emph\>Days\</emph\> is the number of workdays. Positive value for a result after the start date, negative value for a result before the start date.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150693				0	hi	\<emph\>Holidays\</emph\> is a list of optional holidays. These are non-working days. Enter a cell range in which the holidays are listed individually.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150141				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3152782				0	hi	What date came 17 workdays after 1 December 2001? Enter the start date "2001-12-01" in C3 and the number of workdays in D3. Cells F3 to J3 contain the following Christmas and New Year holidays: "2001-12-24", "2001-12-25", "2001-12-26", "2001-12-31", "2002-01-01".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3146142				0	hi	=WORKDAY(C3;D3;F3:J3) returns 2001-12-28. Format the serial date number as a date, for example in the format YYYY-MM-DD.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	समूह				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153088				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080300.xhp\" name=\"Group\"\>Group\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821				0	hi	\<variable id=\"gruppierung\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Group\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Defines the selected cell range as a group of rows or columns.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080300.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069	3			0	hi	When you group a cell range, and outline icon appears in the margins next to the group. To hide or show the group, click the icon. To ungroup the selection, choose \<emph\>Data – Outline -\</emph\> \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080400.xhp\" name=\"Ungroup\"\>\<emph\>Ungroup\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
