helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150237				0	hi	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3146924				0	hi	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151201				0	hi	\<emph\>Price\</emph\> is the price (purchase price) of the security per 100 currency units of par value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156049				0	hi	\<emph\>Redemption\</emph\> is the redemption value per 100 currency units of par value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154139				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3163815				0	hi	A non-interest-bearing security is purchased on 1999-02-15. It matures on 1999-03-01. The price is 99.795 currency units per 100 units of par value, the redemption value is 100 units. The basis is 2. How high is the yield?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155187				0	hi	=YIELDDISC("1999-02-15"; "1999-03-01"; 99.795; 100; 2) returns 0.052823 or 5.2823 per cent.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155140				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>YIELDMAT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rates of return;securities with interest paid on maturity\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155140				0	hi	YIELDMAT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151332				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_YIELDMAT\"\>Calculates the annual yield of a security, the interest of which is paid on the date of maturity.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159100				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3159113				0	hi	YIELDMAT(Settlement; Maturity; Issue; Rate; Price; Basis)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149309				0	hi	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151381				0	hi	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153302				0	hi	\<emph\>Issue\</emph\> is the date of issue of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147140				0	hi	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the interest rate of the security on the issue date.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151067				0	hi	\<emph\>Price\</emph\> is the price (purchase price) of the security per 100 currency units of par value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155342				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3163717				0	hi	A security is purchased on 1999-03-15. It matures on 1999-11-03. The issue date was 1998-11-08. The rate of interest is 6.25%, the price is 100.0123 units. The basis is 0. How high is the yield?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155311				0	hi	=YIELDMAT("1999-03-15"; "1999-11-03"; "1998-11-08"; 0.0625; 100.0123; 0) returns 0.060954 or 6.0954 per cent.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149577				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;annuities\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>annuities\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PMT function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149577				0	hi	PMT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RMZ\"\>Returns the periodic payment for an annuity with constant interest rates.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145257				0	hi	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147278				0	hi	PMT(Rate; NPer; PV; FV; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147291				0	hi	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148641				0	hi	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the number of periods in which annuity is paid.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156360				0	hi	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present value (cash value) in a sequence of payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154920				0	hi	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> (optional) is the desired value (future value) to be reached at the end of the periodic payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156434				0	hi	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) is the due date for the periodic payments. Type=1 is payment at the beginning and Type=0 is payment at the end of each period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_idN11645				0	hi	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152358				0	hi	उदाहरण				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154222				0	hi	What are the periodic payments at a yearly interest rate of 1.99% if the payment time is 3 years and the cash value is 25,000 currency units. There are 36 months as 36 payment periods, and the interest rate per payment period is 1.99%/12.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155943				0	hi	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PMT(1.99%/12;36;25000)\</item\> = -715.96 currency units. The periodic monthly payment is therefore 715.96 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155799				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>TBILLEQ function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>treasury bills;annual return\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>annual return on treasury bills\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
