helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	hi	You can rotate an object around its default pivot point (center point) or a pivot point that you designate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	hi	\<image id=\"img_id3154729\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleobjectrotatemode.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154729\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3150716				0	hi	Select the object you want to rotate. On the \<emph\>Mode\</emph\> toolbar in $[officename] Draw or on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar in $[officename] Impress, click the \<emph\>Rotate\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
