helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_date.xhp	0	help	bm_id5111545				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>inserting;date fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>dates;inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>date fields;fixed/variable\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>fixed dates\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>variable dates\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_date.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155165				0	hi	\<variable id=\"fields_date\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields_date.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Fixed or Variable Date Field\"\>Inserting a Fixed or Variable Date Field\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491				0	hi	You can insert the current date as a field that updates each time you open the document, or as a field that does not update.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3147679				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Document\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	hi	Click “Date” in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list and do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	hi	To insert the date as a field that updates each time you open the document, click ”Date” in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Select\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3154241				0	hi	To insert the date as a field that does not update, click “Date (fixed)” in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Select\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	Indenting Paragraphs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155869				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>formatting; indenting paragraphs\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>indents;in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; indents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hanging indents in paragraphs\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>right indents in paragraphs\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines of text; indents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;indents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	hd_id129398				0	hi	\<variable id=\"indenting\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indenting.xhp\"\>Indenting Paragraphs\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id5589159				0	hi	To change the measurement units, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - General\</item\>, and then select a new measurement unit in the Settings area. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id9936216				0	hi	You can change the indents for the current paragraph, or for all selected paragraphs, or for a Paragraph Style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id7953123				0	hi	You can also \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/ruler.xhp\" name=\"ruler\"\>set indents using the ruler\</link\>. To display the ruler, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Ruler\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id4013794				0	hi	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\</item\> to change the indents for the current paragraph or for all selected paragraphs. You can also \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/ruler.xhp\" name=\"ruler\"\>set indents using the ruler\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id1631824				0	hi	Right-click a paragraph and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit Paragraph Style - Indents & Spacing\</item\> to change the indents for all paragraphs that have the same Paragraph Style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id7271645				0	hi	Indents are calculated with respect to the left and right page margins. If you want the paragraph to extend into the page margin, enter a negative number. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id2136295				0	hi	The indents are different regarding the writing direction. For example, look at the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Before text \</item\>indent value in left-to-right languages. The left edge of the paragraph is indented with respect to the left page margin. In right-to-left languages, the right edge of the paragraph is indented with respect to the right page margin.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id4186223				0	hi	For a hanging indent, enter a positive value for \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Before text\</item\> and a negative value for \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>First line\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indenting.xhp	0	help	par_id1491134				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030100.xhp\"\>Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
