helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154079				0	hi	Select the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Format - Graphics\</emph\>, and then click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05060200.xhp\" name=\"Wrap\"\>\<emph\>Wrap\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153370				0	hi	जिन्हें आप चाहते हैं उन विकल्पों को सेट करें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153386				0	hi	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154247				0	hi	To Change the Wrapping Contour of a Graphic				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154262				0	hi	पाठ जो चारों ओर से घेर लेता है, उसका आकार आप बदल सकते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860				0	hi	Select the graphic, right-click, and then choose \<emph\>Wrap - Edit Contour\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150231				0	hi	Use the tools to draw a new contour, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Apply\</item\> icon (green check mark).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150947				0	hi	Close the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Contour Editor\</item\> window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150520				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05060201.xhp\" name=\"Contour Editor\"\>Contour Editor\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	Master Documents and Subdocuments				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145246				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>master documents;properties\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>subdocuments;properties\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>central documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>subsidiary documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents; master documents and subdocuments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles;master documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145246				0	hi	\<variable id=\"globaldoc\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/globaldoc.xhp\"\>Master Documents and Subdocuments\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3149806				0	hi	A master document lets you manage large documents, such as a book with many chapters. The master document can be seen as a container for individual \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer files. The individual files are called subdocuments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	hd_id6537369				0	hi	Characteristics of Master Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150096				0	hi	When you print a master document, the contents of all subdocuments, indexes, and any text that you entered are printed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153400				0	hi	You can create a table of contents and index in the master document for all of the subdocuments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	hi	Styles that are used in subdocuments, such as new paragraph styles, are automatically imported into the master document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id9033783				0	hi	When viewing the master document, styles that are already present in the master document take precedence over styles with the same name that are imported from subdocuments. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3419598				0	hi	Subdocuments never get changed by changes made to the master document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155180				0	hi	When you add a document to a master document or create a new subdocument, a link is created in the master document. You cannot edit the content of a subdocument directly in the master document, but you can use the Navigator to open any subdocument for edit.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	hd_id7904904				0	hi	Example of Using Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id5817743				0	hi	A master document master.odm consists of some text and links to the subdocuments sub1.odt and sub2.odt. In each subdocument a new paragraph style with the same name Style1 is defined and used, and the subdocuments are saved.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id9169591				0	hi	When you save the master document, the styles from the subdocuments are imported into the master document. First, the new style Style1 from the sub1.odt is imported. Next, the new styles from sub2.odt will be imported, but as Style1 now already is present in the master document, this style from sub2.odt will not be imported. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id1590014				0	hi	In the master document you now see the new style Style1 from the first subdocument. All Style1 paragraphs in the master document will be shown using the Style1 attributes from the first subdocument. However, the second subdocument by itself will not be changed. You see the Style1 paragraphs from the second subdocument with different attributes, depending whether you open the sub2.odt document by itself or as part of the master document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id5878780				0	hi	To avoid confusion, use the same document template for the master document and its subdocuments. This happens automatically when you create the master document and its subdocuments from an existing document with headings, using the command \<emph\>File - Send - Create Master Document\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154382				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator in master mode\"\>Navigator in master mode\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	शॉर्टकट कुंजियों का इस्तेमाल करना ($[officename] राइटर एक्सेसिबिलिटी)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151169				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>keyboard; accessibility $[officename] Writer\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>accessibility; $[officename] Writer\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151169				0	hi	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Using Shortcut Keys ($[officename] Writer Accessibility)\"\>Using Shortcut Keys ($[officename] Writer Accessibility)\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149685				0	hi	Press the keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+<underlined character> to open a menu. In an open menu, press the underlined character to run a command. For example, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+I to open the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> menu, and then T to insert a table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155186				0	hi	कॉन्टेक्स्ट मेन्यू को खोलने के लिए, शिफ़्ट+F10 दबाएँ. कॉन्टेक्स्ट मेन्यू बन्द करने के लिए एस्केप दबाएँ.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155918				0	hi	To Insert Sections				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AA				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Insert\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155870				0	hi	Press F6 until the focus is on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149630				0	hi	Press the right arrow key until the \<emph\>Section\</emph\> icon is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145100				0	hi	Press the down arrow key, and then press the right arrow key to set the width of the section that you want to insert.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156237				0	hi	Press Enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156253				0	hi	Press F6 to place the cursor inside the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153367				0	hi	To Insert Text Tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153388				0	hi	Press F6 until the focus is on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Standard\</item\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154849				0	hi	Press the right arrow key until the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> icon is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	hi	Press the down arrow key, and then use the arrow keys to select the number of columns and rows to include in the table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	hi	Press Enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN1072C				0	hi	Press F6 to place the cursor inside the document.				20200411 15:09:53
