helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149487				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>text frames; inserting/editing/linking\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>resizing;text frames, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scaling; text frames, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>links;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text flow; from frame to frame\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames; linking\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;hiding text frames from printing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149487				0	hi	\<variable id=\"text_frame\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_frame.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\"\>Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149842				0	hi	A text frame is a container for text and graphics that you can place anywhere on a page. You can also use a frame to apply a column layout to text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156104				0	hi	To Insert a Text Frame				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961				0	hi	फ्रेम में शामिल किए जाने वाले पाठ को चुनें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149602				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>, and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145115				0	hi	To Edit a Text Frame				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	hi	पाठ फ्रेम की सामग्री को संपादित करने के लिए, फ्रेम में क्लिक करें तथा जो परिवर्तन आप चाहते हैं उन्हें पूरा करें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156239				0	hi	To edit a frame, select the frame, right-click, and then choose a formatting option. You can also right-click the selected frame, and choose \<emph\>Frame\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156261				0	hi	To resize a text frame, click an edge of the frame, and drag one of the edges or corners of the frame. Hold down Shift while you drag to maintain the proportion of the frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153386				0	hi	To Hide Text From Printing				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154262				0	hi	Any Writer text frame can be set to a mode which allows viewing the text on screen, but hides the text from printing.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154858				0	hi	पाठ फ्रेम को चुनें (आप आठ हैण्डल देखेंगे)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155875				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Format - Frame/Object - Options\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155899				0	hi	In the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> area, unmark the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> check box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148701				0	hi	To Link Text Frames				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149986				0	hi	You can link Writer text frames so that their contents automatically flow from one frame to another.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3153025				0	hi	Click the edge of a frame that you want to link. Selection handles appear on the edges of the frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223	87			0	hi	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Frame\</item\> Bar, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link Frames\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3148968\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_chainframes.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148968\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150930				0	hi	जिस फ्रेम को आप कड़ीबद्ध करना चाहते हैं उसे क्लिक करें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150947				0	hi	आप फ्रेमों को तभी कड़ी दे सकते हैं यदि:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150969				0	hi	लक्ष्य फ्रेम खाली है.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	hi	लक्ष्य फ्रेम अन्य फ्रेम से कड़ीबद्ध नहीं है.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154383				0	hi	The source and the target frames are in the same section. For example, you cannot link a header frame to a footer frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145559				0	hi	स्रोत फ्रेम में अगली कड़ी नहीं है				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145577				0	hi	The target or the source frame are not contained in each other.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3151083				0	hi	When you select a linked frame, a line is displayed that connects the linked frames.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id5853144				0	hi	The AutoSize feature is available only for the last frame in a chain of linked frames.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	पाद-सूचना व शीर्ष-सूचना फ़ॉर्मेट करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154866				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>inserting;lines under headers/above footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines; under headers/above footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>headers;formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers;formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>shadows;headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>borders;for headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154866				0	hi	\<variable id=\"header_with_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_with_line.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Headers or Footers\"\>Formatting Headers or Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3154243				0	hi	You can apply direct formatting to the text in a header or footer. You can also adjust the spacing of the text relative to the header or footer frame or apply a border to the header or footer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155873				0	hi	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page\</item\> and select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Footer\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147109				0	hi	पंक्तियों के बीच की दूरी के विकल्पों को जैसा आप चाहते हैं वैसा सेट करें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147128				0	hi	To add a border or a shadow to the header or the footer, click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>More\</item\>. The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Border/Background\</item\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150520				0	hi	To add a separator line between the header or the footer and the content of the page, click the bottom edge of the square in the \<emph\>Line arrangement\</emph\> area. Click a line style in the \<emph\>Style\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3153742	25			0	hi	To adjust the spacing between the content of the header or footer and the line, clear the \<emph\>Synchronize\</emph\> box, and then enter a value in the\<emph\> Bottom\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	पाठ को सबस्क्रिप्ट या सुपरस्क्रिप्ट बनाना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155174				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>text; subscript and superscript\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>superscript text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>subscript text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>characters;subscript and superscript\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155174				0	hi	\<variable id=\"subscript\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/subscript.xhp\" name=\"Making Text Superscript or Subscript\"\>Making Text Superscript or Subscript\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3155917				0	hi	उस पाठ को चुनें जिसे आप सुपरस्क्रिप्ट या सबस्क्रिप्ट बनाना चाहते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3155865				0	hi	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3149829				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Format - Character - Position\</emph\>, and then select \<emph\>Superscript\</emph\> or \<emph\>Subscript\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3156111				0	hi	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+P to make the text superscript, and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+B to make the text subscript.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020500.xhp\" name=\"Format - Character - Position\"\>Format - Character - Position\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3154705				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"Tools - AutoCorrect - Replace\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect - Replace\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	वर्तनी स्वचालित जाँचें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154265				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>spellcheck;AutoSpellcheck on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic spellcheck\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>checking spelling;while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>words;disabling spellcheck\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154265				0	hi	\<variable id=\"auto_spellcheck\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/auto_spellcheck.xhp\" name=\"Automatically Check Spelling\"\>Automatically Check Spelling\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3154664				0	hi	आपकी टाइपिंग के दौरान ही $[officename] वर्तनी की जाँच स्वचालित रुप से कर सकता है तथा संभावित गलत शब्दों को लहर युक्त लाल रंग की लकीर से रेखांकित करता है.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154678				0	hi	To Check Spelling Automatically While You Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3155531	42			0	hi	मानक पट्टी में स्वचालित वर्तनी जांच सक्रिय करें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3155569	33			0	hi	Right-click a word with a red wavy underline, and then choose a suggested replacement word from the list, or from the \<emph\>AutoCorrect \</emph\>submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147759	6			0	hi	If you choose a word from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>AutoCorrect\</item\> submenu, the underlined word and the replacement word are automatically added to the AutoCorrect list for the current language. To view the AutoCorrect list, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools – AutoCorrect Options\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Replace\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147819				0	hi	You can also add the underlined word to your custom dictionary by choosing \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147220				0	hi	To Exclude Words From the Spellcheck				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147263				0	hi	शब्दों को चुनें जिसे आप अलग रखना चाहते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147282				0	hi	Click the Language control on the Status bar to open a menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3145602				0	hi	Choose “None (Do not check spelling)”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3145648				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010401.xhp\" name=\"Creating a new dictionary.\"\>Creating a new dictionary.\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	पृष्ठ की दिशा बदलना (आड़ा या खड़ा)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	bm_id9683828				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>page styles;orientation/scope\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page formats; changing individual pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; changing individual pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>portrait and landscape\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>landscape and portrait\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;portrait/landscape format\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>orientation of pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paper orientation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages;orientation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sideways orientation of pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scope of page styles\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FF				0	hi	\<variable id=\"pageorientation\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pageorientation.xhp\"\>Changing Page Orientation\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6418042				0	hi	All page properties for Writer text documents, like for example the page orientation, are defined by page styles. By default, a new text document uses the “Default” page style for all pages. If you open an existing text document, different page styles may have been applied to the different pages. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id8324533				0	hi	It is important to know that changes that you apply to a page property will only affect the pages that use the current page style. The current page style is listed in the Status Bar at the lower window border.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7524033				0	hi	To Change the Page Orientation for All Pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6307260				0	hi	If your text document consists only of pages with the same page style, you can change the page properties directly:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id5256508				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id9681997				0	hi	Click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7994323				0	hi	Under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paper format\</item\>, select “Portrait” or “Landscape”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7069002				0	hi	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id4202398				0	hi	To Change the Page Orientation Only for Some Pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071D				0	hi	$[officename] uses page styles to specify the orientation of the pages in a document. Page styles define more page properties, as for example header and footer or page margins. You can either change the “Default” page style for the current document, or you can define own page styles and apply those page styles to any parts of your text. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1449324				0	hi	At the end of this help page, we'll discuss the scope of page styles in detail. If you are unsure about the page style concept, please read the section at the end of this page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1480758				0	hi	Unlike character styles or paragraph styles, the page styles don't know a hierarchy. You can create a new page style based on the properties of an existing page style, but when you later change the source style, the new page style does not automatically inherit the changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2962126				0	hi	To change the page orientation for all pages that share the same page style, you first need a page style, then apply that style:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10727				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10741				0	hi	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	hi	Right-click a page style and choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>. The new page style initially gets all properties of the selected page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	hi	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab page, type a name for the page style in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box, for example "My Landscape".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075D				0	hi	In the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, select the page style that you want to apply to the next page that follows a page with the new style. See the section about the scope of page styles at the end of this help page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10775				0	hi	Click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077D				0	hi	Under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paper format\</item\>, select “Portrait” or “Landscape”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AE				0	hi	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1658375				0	hi	Now you have defined a proper page style with the name "My Landscape". To apply the new style, double-click the "My Landscape" page style in the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window. All pages in the current scope of page styles will be changed. If you defined the "next style" to be a different style, only the first page of the current scope of page styles will be changed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id6082949				0	hi	The Scope of Page Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2858668				0	hi	You should be aware of the scope of page styles in %PRODUCTNAME. Which pages of your text document get affected by editing a page style?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3278603				0	hi	One Page Long Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id5169225				0	hi	A page style can be defined to span one page only. The “First Page” style is an example. You set this property by defining another page style to be the "next style", on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Organizer\</item\> tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6670125				0	hi	A one page long style starts from the lower border of the current page style range up to the next page break. The next page break appears automatically when the text flows to the next page, which is sometimes called a "soft page break". Alternatively, you can insert a manual page break.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2118594				0	hi	To insert a manual page break at the cursor position, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\> or choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Manual Break\</item\> and just click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id166020				0	hi	Manually Defined Range of a Page style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6386913				0	hi	The “Default” page style does not set a different "next style" on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Organizer\</item\> tab page. Instead, the "next style" is set also to be “Default”. All page styles that are followed by the same page style can span multiple pages. The lower and upper borders of the page style range are defined by "page breaks with style". All the pages between any two "page breaks with style" use the same page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6062196				0	hi	You can insert a "page break with style" directly at the cursor position. Alternatively, you can apply the "page break with style" property to a paragraph or to a paragraph style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6054261				0	hi	Perform any one of the following commands:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1811578				0	hi	To insert a "page break with style" at the cursor position, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Manual Break\</item\>, select a \<emph\>Style\</emph\> name from the listbox, and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id9935911				0	hi	To apply the "page break with style" property to the current paragraph, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Paragraph - Text Flow\</item\>. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id4753868				0	hi	To apply the "page break with style" property to the current paragraph style, right-click the current paragraph. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit Paragraph Style\</item\> from the context menu. Click the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id4744407				0	hi	To apply the "page break with style" property to an arbitrary paragraph style, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>. Click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon. Right-click the name of the paragraph style you want to modify and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>. Click the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	मौजूदा पृष्ठ पर आधारित पृष्ठ शैली बनाना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146875				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>headers; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page styles; changing from selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>new page styles from selection\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146875				0	hi	\<variable id=\"change_header\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/change_header.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page\"\>Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153584				0	hi	आप पृष्ठ लेआउट डिज़ाइन कर सकते हैं फिर उस पर आधारित पृष्ठ शैली तैयार कर सकते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3154245				0	hi	For example, you can create a page style that displays a particular header, and another page style that displays a different header.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	hi	Open a new text document, choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3150532				0	hi	Click the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon and select \<emph\>New Styles from Selection\</emph\> from the submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153153				0	hi	Type a name for the page in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style name\</item\> box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153184	32			0	hi	वर्तमान पृष्ठ पर शैली को लागू करने के लिए सूची में नाम को दोहरा क्लिक करें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155541				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and choose the new page style from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155572				0	hi	Type the text that you want in the header. Position the cursor into the main text area outside of the header.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155592				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3147771				0	hi	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page break\</item\> and then select “Default” from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3147810				0	hi	Repeat steps 2-6 to create a second custom page style with a different header.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	नेविगेटर के जरिए हायपरलिंक प्रविष्ट करना				20200411 15:09:53
