helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	फ़ॉन्ट गुण रीसेट करना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149963				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>formats; resetting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>font attributes; resetting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>fonts; resetting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>resetting; fonts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>direct formatting;exiting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;exiting direct formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>exiting;direct formatting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149963				0	hi	\<variable id=\"reset_format\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/reset_format.xhp\" name=\"Resetting Font Attributes\"\>Resetting Font Attributes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3154091				0	hi	You can quickly exit manual formatting by pressing the right-arrow key. For example, if you have pressed Ctrl+B to apply the bold typeface to the text that you type, press the right arrow to return to the default character format of the paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	hi	To reset all direct formatting of existing text, select that text, then choose the menu command \<emph\>Format - Default Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	पाठ का केस बदलना				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155182				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>characters; uppercase or lowercase\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; uppercase or lowercase\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lowercase letters; text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>uppercase; formatting text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>capital letters;changing to small letters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;cases of text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>initial capitals in titles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>small capitals (guide)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155182				0	hi	\<variable id=\"text_capital\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_capital.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Case of Text\"\>Changing the Case of Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3155916				0	hi	You can change the case of text, format text with small capitals, or capitalize the first letter of each word in a selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_idN10728				0	hi	When you apply a formatting to your text by \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>, the text stays the same, it is only displayed in another way. On the other hand, when you choose \<emph\>Format - Change Case\</emph\>, the text is permanently changed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155861				0	hi	To Capitalize Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3147420				0	hi	पाठ को चुनें जिसे आप बड़े अक्षरों में लिखना चाहते हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149841				0	hi	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910485778				0	hi	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Change Case - Uppercase\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910485775				0	hi	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Character\</item\>, click the Font Effects tab, then select the type of capitalization in the Effects box. "Capitals" capitalizes all letters. "Title" capitalizes the first letter of each word. "Small capitals" capitalizes all letters, but in a reduced font size.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149644				0	hi	To Change Text to Lowercase				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149964				0	hi	जिस पाठ को लोअरकेस में बदलना है उसे चुनें.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149606				0	hi	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id112020091049000				0	hi	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Change Case - Lowercase\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910490034				0	hi	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Character\</item\>, click the Font Effects tab, then select "Lowercase" in the Effects box.				20200411 15:09:53
