helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	Cross-references				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153641				0	hi	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"Cross-references\"\>Cross-references\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155142				0	hi	\<variable id=\"reftext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>This is where you insert the references or referenced fields into the current document. References are referenced fields within the same document or within sub-documents of a master document.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3159197				0	hi	The advantage of entering a cross-reference as a field is that you do not have to adjust the references manually every time you change the document. Just update the fields with F9 and the references in the document are updated too.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id4333628				0	hi	Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id4516129				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Lists the available field types. To add a field to your document, click a field type, click a field in the Selection list, and then click Insert.\</ahelp\> The following fields are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3151380				0	hi	Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150700				0	hi	Meaning				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155862				0	hi	संदर्भ सेट करें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3147422				0	hi	Set target for a referenced field. Under \<emph\>Name\</emph\>, enter a name for the reference. When inserting the reference, the name will then appear as an identification in the list box \<emph\>Selection\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149556				0	hi	In an HTML document, reference fields entered this way will be ignored. For the target in HTML documents, you have to \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04040000.xhp\" name=\"insert a bookmark\"\>insert a bookmark\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150548				0	hi	संदर्भ जोड़ें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3147746				0	hi	Inserting a reference to another position in the document. The corresponding text position has to be defined with "Set Reference" first. Otherwise, inserting a reference by choosing a field name under \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> is not possible.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3146344				0	hi	In master documents, you can also reference from one sub-document to another. Note that the reference name will not appear in the selection field and has to be entered "by hand".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149847				0	hi	In an HTML document, reference fields entered this way will be ignored. For referenced fields in HTML documents, you have to \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020400.xhp\" name=\"insert a hyperlink\"\>insert a hyperlink\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id2408825				0	hi	Headings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id9988402				0	hi	The Selection box shows a list of all headings in the order of their appearance in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6401257				0	hi	Numbered Paragraphs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id5841242				0	hi	The Selection box shows a list of all numbered headings and numbered paragraphs in the order of their appearance in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id306711				0	hi	Bookmarks				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150907				0	hi	After inserting a bookmark in the document with \<emph\>Insert - Bookmark\</emph\>, the bookmarks entry on the \<emph\>References\</emph\> tab becomes usable. Bookmarks are used to mark certain text passages in a document. In a text document, you can use the bookmarks, for example, to jump from one passage in the document to another.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155080				0	hi	In an HTML document, these bookmarks become anchors <A name>, which determine the target of hyperlinks for example.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id0818200811011072				0	hi	Footnotes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id0818200811011049				0	hi	If your documents contains a footnote, you can select the Footnotes entry. A reference to a footnote returns the footnote number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6794030				0	hi	(Inserted objects with captions)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7096774				0	hi	You can set references to objects that have captions applied. For example, insert a picture, right-click the picture, choose Caption. Now the object shows up as a numbered "Illustration" in the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154772				0	hi	References are fields. To remove a reference, delete the field. If you set a longer text as a reference and you do not want to reenter it after deleting the reference, select the text and copy it to the clipboard. You can then reinsert it as "unformatted text" at the same position using the command \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>. The text remains intact while the reference is deleted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id5824152				0	hi	Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7374187				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKSELECTION\"\>Lists the available fields for the field type selected in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list. To insert a field, click the field, select a format in the "Insert reference to" list, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7729728				0	hi	To quickly insert a field from the list, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and double-click the field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id2171086				0	hi	In the \<emph\>Insert reference to\</emph\> list, click the format that you want to use.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154333				0	hi	संदर्भ जोड़ें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148786				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_REF:LB_REFFORMAT\"\>Select the format that you want to use for the selected reference field.\</ahelp\> The following formats are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id7576525				0	hi	Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id641193				0	hi	Meaning				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150039				0	hi	Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153134				0	hi	उस पृष्ठ का क्रमांक प्रविष्ट करता है जिसमें संदर्भ लक्ष्य होता है				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150681				0	hi	Reference				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154040				0	hi	Inserts the complete reference target text. For footnotes the footnote number is inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149972				0	hi	ऊपर/नीचे				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149619				0	hi	Inserts "above" or "below", depending on the location of the reference target relative to the position of the reference field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148705				0	hi	पृष्ठ शैली जैसे				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728				0	hi	Inserts the number of the page containing the reference target using the format specified in the page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id5699942				0	hi	Number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6420484				0	hi	Inserts the number of the heading or numbered paragraph, including superior levels depending on the context. See note below this table for more information.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6986602				0	hi	Number (no context)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id616779				0	hi	Inserts only the number of the heading or numbered paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id791039				0	hi	Number (full context)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id1953489				0	hi	Inserts the number of the heading or numbered paragraph, including all superior levels.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154635				0	hi	Chapter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149646				0	hi	उस अध्याय का क्रमांक प्रविष्ट करता है जिसमें संदर्भ लक्ष्य होता है.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155553				0	hi	वर्ग और संख्या				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3155356				0	hi	Inserts the category (caption type) and the number of the reference target. This option is only available when the reference target is an object with a caption.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3154224				0	hi	शीर्षक पाठ				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3145105				0	hi	Inserts the caption label of the reference target. This option is only available when the reference target is an object with a caption.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3149587				0	hi	Numbering				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3146883				0	hi	Inserts the caption number of the reference target. This option is only available when the reference target is an object with a caption.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id757469				0	hi	The "Number" format inserts the number of the heading or numbered paragraph. The superior levels are included depending on the context, as necessary. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id5189062				0	hi	For example, when you are in a chapter 1, subchapter 2, subpart 5, this may be numbered as 1.2.5. When you insert here a reference to text in the previous subpart "1.2.4" and you apply the "Number" format, then the reference will be shown as "4". If in this example the numbering is set to show more sublevels, the same reference will be shown as "2.4" or "1.2.4", depending on the setting. If you use the "Number (full context)" format, you will always see "1.2.4", no matter how the numbered paragraph is formatted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156242				0	hi	Name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156259				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FLD_REF:ED_REFNAME\"\>Type the name of the user-defined field that you want to create.\</ahelp\> To set a target, click "Set Reference" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, type a name in this box, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. To reference the new target, click the target name in the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032	17			0	hi	In a master document, targets that are in different sub-documents are not displayed in the\<emph\> Selection\</emph\> list. If you want to insert a reference to the target, you must type the path and the name in the \<emph\>Name \</emph\>box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id0903200802250745				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the contents that you want to add to a user-defined fields.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3159216				0	hi	If you select text in the document, and then insert a reference, the selected text becomes the contents of the field that you insert.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id6501968				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Edit the value.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\mailmerge07.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	डाक मिलान विज़ॉर्ड - अनुरुप बनाएँ				20200411 15:09:53
