helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	खण्ड प्रविष्ट करें				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154108				0	hi	\<variable id=\"bereicheinfuegen\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Section\"\>Insert Section\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480				0	hi	\<variable id=\"bereich\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"FN_INSERT_COLUMN_SECTION\"\>Inserts a text section at the cursor position in the document. You can also select a block of text and then choose this command to create a section. You can use sections to insert blocks of text from other documents, to apply custom column layouts, or to protect or to hide blocks of text if a condition is met.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152955				0	hi	You can insert an entire document in a section, or a named section from another. You can also insert a section as a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#dde\" name=\"DDE\"\>DDE\</link\> link.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149684				0	hi	To edit a section, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02170000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Sections\"\>\<emph\>Format - Sections\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155183	6			0	hi	The \<emph\>Insert Section \</emph\>dialog contains the following tabs:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151257				0	hi	Insert				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149102				0	hi	उस खण्ड को जिसे आपने पारिभाषित किया है दस्तावेज़ में संकेतक स्थान पर प्रविष्ट करता है.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hi	Hyphenation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154657				0	hi	Hyphenation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148572				0	hi	\<variable id=\"silben\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Inserts hyphens in words that are too long to fit at the end of a line.\</ahelp\> $[officename] searches the document and suggests hyphenation that you can accept or reject. If text is selected, the Hyphenation dialog works on the selected text only. If no text is selected, the Hyphenation dialog works on the whole document.\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153811				0	hi	To automatically hyphenate the current or selected paragraphs, choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph\</emph\>, and then click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>Text Flow\</link\> tab. You can also apply automatic hyphenation to a paragraph style. In text where automatic hyphenation is enabled, the Hyphenation dialog will not find any word to hyphenate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151389				0	hi	जब $[officename] को कोई शब्द मिलता है जिसमें हायफनेशन आवश्यक होता है, निम्न में से कोई एक करें:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155622				0	hi	To accept the hyphenation of the displayed word, click \<emph\>Hyphenate\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154558				0	hi	To change the hyphenation of the displayed word, click the left or right arrow below the word, and then click \<emph\>Hyphenate\</emph\>. The left and right buttons are enabled for words with multiple hyphenation points.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150017				0	hi	To reject the hyphenation of the displayed word, click \<emph\>Skip\</emph\>. This word will not be hyphenated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150018				0	hi	To automatically hyphenate the remaining part of the selection or the document, click \<emph\>Hyphenate All\</emph\> and answer "Yes" to the following question.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150019				0	hi	To end hyphenation, click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>. The hyphenation that is applied already will not be reverted. You can use \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\> to undo all hyphenation that was applied while the Hyphenation dialog was open.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147562				0	hi	To exclude paragraphs from the automatic hyphenation, select the paragraphs, choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph\</emph\>, click the Text Flow tab, and then clear the \<emph\>Automatically\</emph\> check box in the Hyphenation area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154276				0	hi	To disable the Hyphenation dialog and always hyphenate automatically, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010400.xhp\" name=\"Language Settings - Writing Aids\"\>Language Settings - Writing Aids\</link\>\</emph\>, and select the \<emph\>Hyphenate without inquiry\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152950				0	hi	To manually enter a hyphen directly in the document, click in the word where you want to add the hyphen, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Minus sign (-).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147523				0	hi	To insert a non-breaking (protected) hyphen directly in the document, click in the word that you want to hyphenate, and then press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>+Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Minus sign(-).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154573				0	hi	To hide custom hyphens, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040600.xhp\" name=\"Text Document - Formatting Aids\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</link\>\</emph\>, and then clear the \<emph\>Custom hyphens\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150360				0	hi	Word				20200411 15:09:53
