helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148768				0	hi	\<bookmark_value\>editing; concordance files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>concordance files; definition\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148768				0	hi	Edit Concordance File				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3151180				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_CREATE_AUTOMARK\"\>Create or edit a list of words to include in an Alphabetical Index.\</ahelp\> A concordance file lists words that should be referenced in an alphabetical index, together with the page number(s) where they appear in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id837427				0	hi	You can use the Find All button on the Find & Replace dialog to highlight all places where a word appears, then open the Insert Index Entry dialog to add that word and places to the alphabetical index. However, if you need the same set of alphabetical indexes in multiple documents, the concordance file allows to enter every word just once, then use the list many times.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154645				0	hi	कॉन्कार्डेंस फ़ाइल संपादन संवाद पर पहुँचने के लिए:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3149292				0	hi	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Indexes and Tables - Index/Table\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420	21			0	hi	In the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>box, select "Alphabetical Index".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3154107	22			0	hi	In the \<emph\>Options \</emph\>area, select the \<emph\>Concordance file\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3153668				0	hi	Click the \<emph\>File\</emph\> button, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\> or \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3154470	24			0	hi	कॉन्कार्डेंस फ़ाइल में निम्न क्षेत्र होते हैं:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3152953				0	hi	"Search term" refers to the index entry that you want to mark in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	hi	"वैकल्पिक प्रविष्टि" उस निर्देशिका प्रविष्टि को संदर्भित करती है जिसे आप चाहते हैं कि निर्देशिका में दिखाई दे.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3154194				0	hi	The 1st and 2nd Keys are parent index entries. The "Search term" or the "Alternative entry" appears as a subentry under the 1st and 2nd Keys.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155184				0	hi	"Match case" means that uppercase and lowercase letters are considered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3143282				0	hi	"सिर्फ शब्द" से वाक्यांश को एक शब्द के रुप में ढूंढता है.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3147220				0	hi	To enable the "Match case" or "Word only" options, click in the corresponding cell, and then select the check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153629				0	hi	कॉनकार्डेंस संपादन फ़ाइल संवाद के बगैर कॉनकार्डेंस फ़ाइल तैयार करने के लिए:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3153644				0	hi	जब आप कॉनकॉर्डेंस फ़ाइल बनाते हैं तो निम्न फ़ॉर्मेट गाइडलाइन का इस्तेमाल करें:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3152770				0	hi	कॉनकॉर्डेंस फ़ाइल में प्रत्येक सूची अलग पंक्ति में है.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155142				0	hi	कमेंटेड पंक्तियाँ # से प्रारंभ होती हैं.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3153354				0	hi	प्रविष्टियों के लिए निम्न फ़ॉर्मेट इस्तेमाल करें:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3149172				0	hi	Search term;Alternative entry;1st key;2nd key;Match case;Word only				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3156270				0	hi	The entries "Match case" and "Word only" are interpreted as "No" or FALSE if they are empty or zero (0). All other contents are interpreted as "Yes" or TRUE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145778				0	hi	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907				0	hi	For example, to include the word "Boston" in your alphabetical index under the "Cities" entry, enter the following line in the concordance file:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370				0	hi	Boston;Boston;Cities;;0;0 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3151383				0	hi	This also finds "Boston" if it is written in lowercase letters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155866				0	hi	To include the "Beacon Hill" district in Boston under the "Cities" entry, enter the following line:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3150116	18			0	hi	Beacon Hill;Boston;Cities; 				20200411 15:09:53
