helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154571				0	hi	\<variable id=\"autotexttext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:EditGlossary\"\>Creates, edits, or inserts AutoText. You can store formatted text, text with graphics, tables, and fields as AutoText. To quickly insert AutoText, type the shortcut for the AutoText in your document, and then press F3.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143277				0	hi	You can also click the arrow next to the \<emph\>AutoText\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> bar, and then choose the AutoText that you want to insert.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148982				0	hi	AutoText				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153640	5			0	hi	The \<emph\>AutoText \</emph\>dialog lists the AutoText categories and entries.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152766				0	hi	टाइपिंग के समय के सुझाव के अनुसार नाम का बचा भाग दिखाएँ				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145758				0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:DLG_GLOSSARY:CB_INSERT_TIP\"\>Displays a suggestion for completing a word as a Help Tip after you type the first three letters of a word that matches an AutoText entry. To accept the suggestion, press Enter. If more than one AutoText entry matches the letters that you type, press Ctrl+Tab to advance through the entries.\</ahelp\> For example, to insert dummy text, type "Dum", and then press Enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177	53			0	hi	To display the list in reverse order, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+Tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151378				0	hi	Name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155862	10			0	hi	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:DLG_GLOSSARY:ED_NAME\"\>Lists the name of the currently selected AutoText entry. If you have selected text in the document, type the name of the new AutoText entry, click the \<emph\>AutoText \</emph\>button, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150113				0	hi	Shortcut				20200411 15:09:53
